1
00:00:14,440 --> 00:00:18,240
An evil old house , the kind some people call haunted ...

2
00:00:19,120 --> 00:00:22,280
is like an undiscovered country waiting to be explored .

3
00:00:23,360 --> 00:00:27,120
Hill House had stood for 90 years and might stand for 90 more .

4
00:00:28,240 --> 00:00:32,000
Silence lay steadily against the wood and stone of Hill House .

5
00:00:32,720 --> 00:00:35,840
Whatever walked there walked alone .

6
00:02:07,560 --> 00:02:10,560
Scandal , murder , insanity , suicide .

7
00:02:11,040 --> 00:02:13,440
The history of Hill House was ideal .

8
00:02:13,520 --> 00:02:15,520
It had everything I wanted .

9
00:02:16,520 --> 00:02:19,240
It was built 90-odd , very odd years ago ...

10
00:02:19,280 --> 00:02:22,720
by a man named Hugh Crain as a home for his wife and daughter ...

11
00:02:22,800 --> 00:02:25,640
in the most remote part of New England he could find .

12
00:02:30,160 --> 00:02:32,200
It was an evil house from the beginning .

13
00:02:32,280 --> 00:02:34,240
A house that was born bad .

14
00:02:41,520 --> 00:02:42,880
Hugh Crain 's young wife ...

15
00:02:42,960 --> 00:02:46,000
died seconds before she was to set eyes on the house .

16
00:02:47,240 --> 00:02:50,080
She was killed when , for no apparent reason ...

17
00:02:50,120 --> 00:02:53,720
the horses bolted , crashing her carriage against a big tree .

18
00:02:59,760 --> 00:03:01,480
Mrs. Crain was carried ...

19
00:03:02,520 --> 00:03:04,840
lifeless is the word , I think ...

20
00:03:04,880 --> 00:03:07,680
into the home her husband had built for her .

21
00:03:08,920 --> 00:03:11,560
Hugh Crain was left an embittered man ...

22
00:03:12,240 --> 00:03:15,080
with a small daughter , Abigail , to bring up .

23
00:03:32,880 --> 00:03:35,280
Fortunately , for me , that is ...

24
00:03:35,800 --> 00:03:38,920
Hugh Crain did not leave Hill House . He married again .

25
00:03:47,400 --> 00:03:50,440
The second Mrs. Crain 's death was even more interesting ...

26
00:03:50,520 --> 00:03:52,360
than her predecessor 's .

27
00:04:05,480 --> 00:04:08,640
I 've been unable to find out how or why she fell ...

28
00:04:09,200 --> 00:04:11,240
although I have my suspicions .

29
00:04:17,800 --> 00:04:20,840
Hugh Crain left Abigail with a nurse and went to England ...

30
00:04:20,920 --> 00:04:23,320
where he died in a drowning accident .

31
00:04:23,400 --> 00:04:24,600
Marvelous !

32
00:04:24,680 --> 00:04:28,640
I mean , the way the history of Hill House follows a classic pattern .

33
00:04:31,880 --> 00:04:32,920
For some reason ...

34
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:36,680
Abigail kept that same nursery room in Hill House where she grew up ...

35
00:04:37,480 --> 00:04:38,920
and grew old .

36
00:04:53,440 --> 00:04:56,360
In later years , she became a bedridden invalid .

37
00:04:56,800 --> 00:05:00,520
She took a girl from the village to live with her as a paid companion .

38
00:05:04,080 --> 00:05:05,800
It 's with this young companion ...

39
00:05:05,880 --> 00:05:08,800
the evil reputation of Hill House really begins .

40
00:05:14,880 --> 00:05:17,760
The story goes that the old lady died calling for help ...

41
00:05:17,840 --> 00:05:19,800
in the nursery upstairs ...

42
00:05:20,040 --> 00:05:23,720
while the companion fooled around with a farm hand on the verandah .

43
00:05:34,280 --> 00:05:38,200
The companion inherited Hill House and occupied it for many years .

44
00:05:38,320 --> 00:05:41,160
The local people believe that , one way or another ...

45
00:05:41,200 --> 00:05:43,440
she had murdered her benefactor .

46
00:05:43,960 --> 00:05:47,160
She lived a life of complete solitude in the empty house ...

47
00:05:47,240 --> 00:05:50,160
though some say that the house was not empty ...

48
00:05:50,240 --> 00:05:53,600
and never has been since the night old Miss Abby died .

49
00:05:54,800 --> 00:05:58,960
They say that whatever there was and still is in the house ...

50
00:05:59,760 --> 00:06:02,120
eventually drove the companion mad .

51
00:06:05,960 --> 00:06:08,000
We do know she hanged herself .

52
00:06:08,520 --> 00:06:09,600
After her death ...

53
00:06:09,640 --> 00:06:13,400
the house passed legally into the hands of a distant relative in Boston ...

54
00:06:13,480 --> 00:06:17,880
an old lady , Mrs. Sannerson , who I very much wanted to see .

55
00:06:18,960 --> 00:06:22,280
All my life I 've been looking for an honestly haunted house .

56
00:06:22,320 --> 00:06:26,120
In the interests of psychic research , you must let me have it for a few weeks .

57
00:06:26,160 --> 00:06:30,320
No one who rented Hill House ever stayed for more than a few days .

58
00:06:31,400 --> 00:06:34,600
The dead are not quiet in Hill House .

59
00:06:34,920 --> 00:06:36,400
I don 't believe it .

60
00:06:36,480 --> 00:06:38,640
Dr. Markway is a trained anthropologist ...

61
00:06:38,720 --> 00:06:40,960
a respected member of a university faculty .

62
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:43,520
We should welcome such a man to investigate Hill House .

63
00:06:43,560 --> 00:06:44,640
Perhaps .

64
00:06:44,680 --> 00:06:47,480
As an old woman due shortly to enter the next world ...

65
00:06:47,560 --> 00:06:49,120
I 'd like to know if there is one .

66
00:06:49,160 --> 00:06:52,960
I 'm sure his report will give Hill House a clean bill of health .

67
00:06:53,360 --> 00:06:57,160
How will you go about conducting your investigations , Dr. Markway ?

68
00:06:57,880 --> 00:07:01,240
I shall occupy the house with a group of carefully selected assistants ...

69
00:07:01,320 --> 00:07:03,840
- Assistants ? - My dear Mrs. Sannerson ...

70
00:07:04,200 --> 00:07:07,040
I am a scientist conducting an unusual experiment .

71
00:07:07,120 --> 00:07:09,600
A haunted house . Everyone laughs .

72
00:07:09,680 --> 00:07:11,840
So I must have specially qualified help ...

73
00:07:11,920 --> 00:07:15,240
to take notes and document any evidence of the supernatural I may find .

74
00:07:15,280 --> 00:07:18,280
- Who are these assistants ? - I haven 't made my final choice yet ...

75
00:07:18,360 --> 00:07:21,480
but they 're from a list of names I 've been assembling over the years .

76
00:07:21,560 --> 00:07:24,320
- We don 't want any publicity seekers . - Of course not .

77
00:07:24,360 --> 00:07:27,520
These people have only been selected after painstaking research .

78
00:07:27,600 --> 00:07:31,360
They 've all been involved before , one way or another , with the abnormal .

79
00:07:31,400 --> 00:07:33,240
I don 't like the sound of that .

80
00:07:33,320 --> 00:07:36,600
- Are any of the people women ? - Some .

81
00:07:36,680 --> 00:07:38,760
- Are you a married man ? - Yes .

82
00:07:39,080 --> 00:07:41,600
Then your wife will be accompanying you .

83
00:07:41,680 --> 00:07:43,160
I 'm afraid not .

84
00:07:43,240 --> 00:07:46,480
My wife disapproves of my experiments with the supernatural .

85
00:07:46,560 --> 00:07:48,520
She wants no part of Hill House .

86
00:07:48,600 --> 00:07:51,320
To make sure that everything is as it should be ...

87
00:07:51,400 --> 00:07:54,120
suppose your nephew goes along with Dr. Markway ?

88
00:07:54,200 --> 00:07:55,160
Luke ?

89
00:07:55,840 --> 00:07:58,360
Our young Lochinvar from out of the Midwest .

90
00:07:59,400 --> 00:08:02,320
I haven 't much confidence in that branch of the family .

91
00:08:02,400 --> 00:08:05,880
In this case , I think you can . Luke expects to inherit Hill House ...

92
00:08:05,960 --> 00:08:08,760
and he 'll make sure that his property is well taken care of .

93
00:08:08,840 --> 00:08:10,080
His property ?

94
00:08:11,560 --> 00:08:14,400
Still , it might be rather good at that .

95
00:08:14,960 --> 00:08:17,960
Luke hopes one day to live off Hill House .

96
00:08:18,040 --> 00:08:21,120
But he never dreamed to find himself living in it .

97
00:08:21,880 --> 00:08:24,520
Harper , give Dr. Markway his lease .

98
00:08:24,600 --> 00:08:26,080
Thank you , Mrs. Sannerson .

99
00:08:26,160 --> 00:08:29,080
A word of warning : Don 't play gin with Luke .

100
00:08:29,160 --> 00:08:30,320
He 's a cardsharp .

101
00:08:30,400 --> 00:08:33,240
Good . That indicates a strong instinct for self-preservation .

102
00:08:33,320 --> 00:08:37,400
Exactly what do you and your assistants expect to find at Hill House ?

103
00:08:38,680 --> 00:08:41,880
Maybe only a few loose floorboards , and maybe ...

104
00:08:42,440 --> 00:08:44,120
I only say maybe ...

105
00:08:44,760 --> 00:08:46,680
the key to another world .

106
00:09:05,800 --> 00:09:08,040
You 've just got to let me have the car .

107
00:09:08,480 --> 00:09:11,040
There 's no other way of getting there , and I 'm expected .

108
00:09:11,120 --> 00:09:13,640
- Calm down . - I 've even bought some new clothes .

109
00:09:13,720 --> 00:09:15,080
Please , Bud .

110
00:09:15,520 --> 00:09:19,240
Carrie drives the car all the time and I never even take it out of the garage .

111
00:09:19,320 --> 00:09:21,480
- Mother ... - Mother what ?

112
00:09:23,560 --> 00:09:24,880
Nothing .

113
00:09:29,400 --> 00:09:31,280
Auntie Nell is blinking .

114
00:09:33,800 --> 00:09:35,160
Quiet , Dora .

115
00:09:35,520 --> 00:09:38,640
Let 's talk this over without anybody getting emotional or nervous .

116
00:09:38,720 --> 00:09:40,680
Why shouldn 't I be nervous ?

117
00:09:40,760 --> 00:09:44,200
My first chance for a vacation in my life and you won 't let me take it .

118
00:09:44,280 --> 00:09:47,080
There 's a good reason Mother was afraid for you to go anywhere ...

119
00:09:47,160 --> 00:09:48,320
and it still applies .

120
00:09:48,400 --> 00:09:51,800
We 're not going to dig up the family skeleton again , are we ?

121
00:09:52,080 --> 00:09:54,400
I think you should have a vacation , Nell .

122
00:09:54,440 --> 00:09:57,880
Nobody knows better than me what you went through during your mother 's illness .

123
00:09:57,960 --> 00:10:00,800
Dirty laundry , the smell of that sickroom ...

124
00:10:01,080 --> 00:10:03,080
Talk about mean old ladies !

125
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:05,920
