224
00:19:32,320 --> 00:19:33,760
How very nice .

225
00:19:34,080 --> 00:19:36,960
I set dinner on the dining room sideboard at 6 : 00 .

226
00:19:37,040 --> 00:19:38,640
I clear up in the morning .

227
00:19:38,720 --> 00:19:42,160
I have breakfast for you at 9 : 00 . I don 't wait on people .

228
00:19:42,360 --> 00:19:44,960
I don 't stay after I set out the dinner .

229
00:19:45,080 --> 00:19:47,280
Not after it begins to get dark .

230
00:19:47,800 --> 00:19:49,760
I leave before the dark comes .

231
00:19:50,360 --> 00:19:53,240
- Your husband ? - We live over in town , miles away .

232
00:19:53,480 --> 00:19:55,640
So there won 't be anyone around if you need help .

233
00:19:55,720 --> 00:19:56,800
I understand .

234
00:19:56,880 --> 00:19:59,280
We couldn 't hear you ... in the night .

235
00:20:00,120 --> 00:20:02,720
- Do you have any idea when ... - No one could .

236
00:20:03,080 --> 00:20:05,120
No one lives any nearer than town .

237
00:20:05,880 --> 00:20:08,280
No one will come any nearer than that ...

238
00:20:08,360 --> 00:20:09,520
I know .

239
00:20:10,040 --> 00:20:12,960
... in the night , in the dark .

240
00:20:38,800 --> 00:20:42,240
I 'm like a small creature swallowed whole by a monster ...

241
00:20:42,680 --> 00:20:45,640
and the monster feels my tiny movements inside .

242
00:20:50,600 --> 00:20:53,080
Now , Eleanor Lance , you just stop it .

243
00:21:28,640 --> 00:21:30,320
There 's no one else they could get . I set dinner on the ...

244
00:21:30,360 --> 00:21:32,520
Thank heavens somebody 's here .

245
00:21:32,800 --> 00:21:35,720
My name 's Eleanor Lance . I 'm so glad you 're here .

246
00:21:35,800 --> 00:21:37,840
I 'm Theodora . Just Theodora .

247
00:21:38,120 --> 00:21:39,640
What about this crazy house ?

248
00:21:39,720 --> 00:21:41,960
I 'm right next door . We have a connecting bath .

249
00:21:42,000 --> 00:21:43,800
This used to be the embalming room , I bet .

250
00:21:43,880 --> 00:21:45,200
It was terrible being here alone .

251
00:21:45,240 --> 00:21:47,040
I set dinner on the sideboard at 6 : 00 ...

252
00:21:47,120 --> 00:21:49,200
Where 's Markway ? I thought he 'd be here first .

253
00:21:49,280 --> 00:21:51,080
Serve yourselves . I clear up in the morning .

254
00:21:51,120 --> 00:21:53,640
- Have you known Dr. Markway long ? - Breakfast is at 9 : 00 .

255
00:21:53,680 --> 00:21:56,640
- I 've never met him . - I don 't stay after 6 : 00 , when it gets dark .

256
00:21:56,720 --> 00:22:01,120
Our only contact is our correspondence about the " experiment . "

257
00:22:01,200 --> 00:22:02,560
I leave before the dark comes .

258
00:22:02,640 --> 00:22:05,640
So there won 't be anyone around if you need help .

259
00:22:06,600 --> 00:22:08,800
No one can hear you if you scream in the night .

260
00:22:08,880 --> 00:22:10,640
Isn 't that so , Mrs. Dudley ?

261
00:22:10,920 --> 00:22:13,240
No one lives any nearer than town .

262
00:22:13,800 --> 00:22:16,360
No one will come any nearer than that ...

263
00:22:16,440 --> 00:22:18,840
in the night ... in the dark .

264
00:22:25,120 --> 00:22:27,360
- You 're frightened , Nell . - No more .

265
00:22:27,760 --> 00:22:30,280
Just when I thought I was all alone .

266
00:22:30,760 --> 00:22:32,800
But how did you know my nickname is Nell ?

267
00:22:32,880 --> 00:22:35,600
That is the affectionate term for Eleanor , isn 't it ?

268
00:22:35,680 --> 00:22:37,760
Yes , I suppose it is .

269
00:22:38,680 --> 00:22:40,560
What a nice way of putting it .

270
00:22:40,640 --> 00:22:43,200
The affectionate term for Theodora is Theo .

271
00:22:45,000 --> 00:22:47,280
We 're going to be great friends , Theo .

272
00:22:47,320 --> 00:22:48,720
Like sisters ?

273
00:22:50,000 --> 00:22:52,040
There 's no need to hang around our rooms .

274
00:22:52,080 --> 00:22:53,880
- Let 's go exploring . - I 'd like to .

275
00:22:53,960 --> 00:22:57,680
Why don 't you put on one of your new things ? Something that 'll stand out .

276
00:22:57,720 --> 00:23:01,400
I think it 's a good idea around here to always remain strictly visible .

277
00:23:01,600 --> 00:23:03,280
Be ready in a jiffy .

278
00:23:04,080 --> 00:23:06,200
How did you know I brought new clothes ?

279
00:23:06,280 --> 00:23:08,760
You wear your thoughts on your sleeve .

280
00:23:08,840 --> 00:23:11,000
Anyway , that 's better than my heart .

281
00:23:23,360 --> 00:23:26,640
How did I get into this ? Why am I here ?

282
00:23:27,600 --> 00:23:29,520
What nightmares are waiting ?

283
00:23:29,600 --> 00:23:33,400
Damn it ! I still say one of these doors should lead to the main hall .

284
00:23:33,480 --> 00:23:35,400
Any lights near you , Nell ?

285
00:23:39,120 --> 00:23:41,160
It helps if you make a game of it .

286
00:23:41,200 --> 00:23:43,240
Pretend this is hide-and-seek .

287
00:23:43,280 --> 00:23:44,840
But we 're still lost .

288
00:23:45,440 --> 00:23:46,440
Yes .

289
00:23:47,320 --> 00:23:50,280
That passageway . We haven 't tried that one yet .

290
00:23:51,480 --> 00:23:53,080
What 's the matter ?

291
00:23:54,160 --> 00:23:56,120
There 's something with us .

292
00:23:57,880 --> 00:23:59,600
I don 't see anything .

293
00:23:59,720 --> 00:24:01,560
- Can 't you feel it ? - No .

294
00:24:03,120 --> 00:24:04,600
I feel a chill .

295
00:24:05,120 --> 00:24:08,280
- It 's moving . - It 's just the air rushing past our ears .

296
00:24:10,160 --> 00:24:11,280
Then who ?

297
00:24:13,400 --> 00:24:14,360
What ?

298
00:24:15,280 --> 00:24:18,280
The house , it 's alive .

299
00:24:26,640 --> 00:24:28,360
She didn 't hear that .

300
00:24:29,440 --> 00:24:31,280
Nobody heard it but me .

301
00:24:35,000 --> 00:24:36,680
It wants you , Nell .

302
00:24:37,800 --> 00:24:39,560
The house is calling you .

303
00:24:46,760 --> 00:24:51,080
I 've waited such a long time . Is this what I came so far to find ?

304
00:24:55,320 --> 00:24:58,360
Don 't let me go ! Theo , stay with me !

305
00:25:00,560 --> 00:25:03,680
You won 't believe this , but five minutes ago I left this door open ...

306
00:25:03,760 --> 00:25:06,720
so you could find your way . It closed by itself .

307
00:25:07,400 --> 00:25:09,800
Welcome to Hill House . I 'm Dr. Markway .

308
00:25:09,880 --> 00:25:13,680
Thank goodness . I thought you might be a ghost .

309
00:25:14,240 --> 00:25:17,040
- How do you know I 'm not ? - Don 't be ghoulish .

310
00:25:17,520 --> 00:25:19,800
You mustn 't confuse ghoulish and ghostly .

311
00:25:19,880 --> 00:25:22,600
The word " ghoulish " is used to describe a feeling of horror ...

312
00:25:22,680 --> 00:25:24,520
often accompanied by intense cold .

313
00:25:24,560 --> 00:25:26,880
It has nothing to do with ghosts . Ghosts are visible .

314
00:25:26,960 --> 00:25:30,440
- Enough of that . Get us out of here fast . - What 's the matter ?

315
00:25:31,520 --> 00:25:33,600
Let 's just say we 're scared of the dark .

316
00:25:33,680 --> 00:25:36,200
I , too , go in mortal terror of the dark .

317
00:25:37,760 --> 00:25:40,160
- I 'm Theodora . - You must be Eleanor .

318
00:25:40,320 --> 00:25:41,760
I 'm unsure at the moment .

319
00:25:41,840 --> 00:25:43,920
If it turns out you 're not , I 'll be disappointed .

320
00:25:44,000 --> 00:25:45,160
All right .

321
00:25:45,280 --> 00:25:49,200
It 's Theo who 's wearing velvet , so I must be Eleanor in tweed .

322
00:25:49,360 --> 00:25:50,280
Good .

323
00:25:50,320 --> 00:25:53,240
Follow me through the uncharted waste of Hill House .

324
00:25:53,320 --> 00:25:54,880
Dinner 's waiting .

325
00:25:59,520 --> 00:26:02,120
- Do you like it ? - Lovely . What do you call this ?

326
00:26:02,200 --> 00:26:03,800
The Purple Parlor .

327
00:26:04,000 --> 00:26:06,880
We 're going to use this as the operating room .

328
00:26:08,120 --> 00:26:10,000
I mean the center of operations .

329
00:26:10,080 --> 00:26:12,440
- It 's not very cheerful . - I don 't know .

330
00:26:12,520 --> 00:26:14,840
There 's nothing more cozy than an old gargoyle ...

331
00:26:14,920 --> 00:26:16,800
except maybe a whipping post or two .

332
00:26:16,880 --> 00:26:19,560
This house does have its little oddities .

333
00:26:19,880 --> 00:26:22,080
The man who built it was a misfit ...

334
00:26:22,160 --> 00:26:25,000
who hated people and their conventional ideas .

335
00:26:25,080 --> 00:26:27,520
He built his house to suit his mind .

336
00:26:27,720 --> 00:26:31,520
For instance , all the doors are hung slightly off-center .

337
00:26:31,920 --> 00:26:34,720
Probably explains why they keep swinging shut by themselves .

338
00:26:34,800 --> 00:26:35,920
Watch .

339
00:26:37,160 --> 00:26:38,560
Now watch this .

340
00:26:44,240 --> 00:26:45,880
What did I tell you ?

341
00:26:47,320 --> 00:26:51,080
Anyway , all the angles are slightly off . There isn 't a square corner in the place .

342
00:26:51,160 --> 00:26:53,960
No wonder it 's impossible to find your way around .

343
00:26:54,040 --> 00:26:56,520
Add up all these wrong angles ...

344
00:26:56,600 --> 00:26:59,440
and you get one big distortion in the house as a whole .

345
00:26:59,520 --> 00:27:01,840
Clever , Eleanor . You catch on fast .

346
00:27:02,640 --> 00:27:03,880
I 'm hungry .

347
00:27:04,640 --> 00:27:05,680
Let 's go .

348
00:27:05,960 --> 00:27:08,360
Sorry . In the psychic world we 're apt to forget ...

349
00:27:08,440 --> 00:27:12,080
that food is still the main concern of poor old homo sapiens .

350
00:27:12,520 --> 00:27:14,720
You see ? Closed by itself .

351
00:27:16,840 --> 00:27:19,000
To the right , ladies .

352
00:27:26,280 --> 00:27:27,960
Now , which door ?

353
00:27:30,200 --> 00:27:31,560
- That one . - Wrong .

354
00:27:31,640 --> 00:27:33,720
I 've studied a map , it 's this one .

355
00:27:36,240 --> 00:27:39,560
- This proves it , one of you is a witch . - A broom closet .

356
00:27:39,640 --> 00:27:42,280
If you can 't find your way around , how will we ever ?

357
00:27:42,320 --> 00:27:45,880
All these doors , it makes me think of the lady and the tiger .

358
00:27:45,960 --> 00:27:48,560
Let 's see if there 's a tiger behind this one .

359
00:27:56,400 --> 00:27:57,600
That 's funny .

360
00:27:58,080 --> 00:27:59,680
- No tiger ? - Listen .

361
00:28:09,000 --> 00:28:11,240
What 's wrong ? Too much vermouth ?

362
00:28:11,520 --> 00:28:12,960
Nothing that serious ...

363
00:28:13,040 --> 00:28:16,960
and , please , no cracks about my passion for spirits .

364
00:28:18,240 --> 00:28:20,800
If you two are the ghostly inhabitants of Hill House ...

365
00:28:20,880 --> 00:28:22,840
I must confess I 'm glad I came .

366
00:28:24,120 --> 00:28:26,040
It has taken 60 million years ...

367
00:28:26,120 --> 00:28:28,880
to develop the carnivorous biped you see before you .

368
00:28:29,080 --> 00:28:30,080
Luke Sannerson .

369
00:28:30,120 --> 00:28:32,200
Let 's see what kind of martinis it makes .

370
00:28:32,280 --> 00:28:35,440
They should be pretty good . I majored in them at college .

371
00:28:35,520 --> 00:28:38,760
Are we to expect any more carnivorous bipeds ?

372
00:28:39,160 --> 00:28:42,240
Originally , there were six committed to the experiment ...

373
00:28:42,320 --> 00:28:44,120
but one by one the others dropped out .

374
00:28:44,200 --> 00:28:48,360
I suppose they were frightened by the various unsavory stories about the house .

375
00:28:49,720 --> 00:28:51,680
You 're the only ones left .

376
00:28:52,200 --> 00:28:53,360
What stories ?

377
00:28:53,440 --> 00:28:55,840
You didn 't investigate before you came here ?

378
00:28:57,680 --> 00:28:59,080
So much the better .

379
00:28:59,120 --> 00:29:01,600
You should be innocent and receptive .

380
00:29:03,520 --> 00:29:06,280
- So let 's drink to our success . - Success ?

381
00:29:06,760 --> 00:29:10,080
And just how do you reckon success in a junket like this ?

382
00:29:10,120 --> 00:29:11,840
I 'd like to drink ...

383
00:29:12,680 --> 00:29:14,920
to just us , good companions .

384
00:29:15,240 --> 00:29:16,480
Excellent .

385
00:29:17,640 --> 00:29:19,120
To my new companion .

386
00:29:21,280 --> 00:29:23,040
Except I don 't drink .

387
00:29:29,920 --> 00:29:32,440
- I think I 'll have some more salmon . - Palissy .

388
00:29:32,880 --> 00:29:34,760
- Yeah ? How much is it worth ? - Plenty .

389
00:29:34,800 --> 00:29:37,440
Haven 't seen Palissy outside of a museum .

390
00:29:37,680 --> 00:29:40,760
I 'll take a pair of Kastle skis for them any day of the week .

391
00:29:40,840 --> 00:29:43,400
I wonder how much I 'll get for this New England fossil .

392
00:29:43,480 --> 00:29:47,680
Don 't let Mrs. Dudley hear you saying that . At the moment she 's giving us the best .

393
00:29:47,760 --> 00:29:51,800
I 'm a simple fellow myself , easily satisfied by the best of everything .

394
00:29:51,880 --> 00:29:54,240
Including , I hope , some startling events to come .

395
00:29:54,280 --> 00:29:57,000
Exactly what do you expect to happen , Dr. Markway ?

396
00:29:57,360 --> 00:29:59,640
Yes , what is the matter with Hill House ?

397
00:29:59,800 --> 00:30:02,160
What 's going to happen ? Why are we here ?

398
00:30:03,880 --> 00:30:08,160
Like so many people through the ages , I 've been intrigued by the supernatural ...

399
00:30:08,240 --> 00:30:11,000
or rather the possibility of the supernatural .

400
00:30:11,440 --> 00:30:13,880
I 'm here in hopes of proving its existence .

401
00:30:13,920 --> 00:30:17,200
You 're here to keep track and take notes for an authenticated record .

402
00:30:17,280 --> 00:30:19,640
- Okay . But why us ? - It 's no accident .

403
00:30:20,040 --> 00:30:23,560
You 're what 's left of a select company chosen with great care .

404
00:30:23,640 --> 00:30:25,760
I combed the records of psychic societies ...

405
00:30:25,840 --> 00:30:29,240
the back numbers of newspapers , reports of parapsychologists ...

406
00:30:29,280 --> 00:30:33,160
hoping to find people who 've been touched in some way by the supernatural .

407
00:30:33,440 --> 00:30:37,120
It 's my belief that the very presence of people like yourselves in this house ...

408
00:30:37,160 --> 00:30:40,280
will help to stimulate the strange forces at work here .

409
00:30:40,320 --> 00:30:42,680
Charming thought , to be used as live bait .

410
00:30:42,720 --> 00:30:45,720
I 'm here because I 'm a wolf in ghost 's clothing .

411
00:30:45,920 --> 00:30:48,920
I 'm not really running a psychic beauty contest .

412
00:30:49,440 --> 00:30:50,760
You 're here , Theo ...

413
00:30:50,840 --> 00:30:53,920
because of your remarkable powers of extrasensory perception .

414
00:30:54,000 --> 00:30:56,640
ESP ? Don 't believe in it .

415
00:30:57,040 --> 00:30:58,400
Theo 's a champ .

416
00:30:58,480 --> 00:31:01,920
Her name shines in the annals of Duke University Psychic Lab ...

417
00:31:02,000 --> 00:31:04,360
where she identified 19 out of 20 cards ...

418
00:31:04,440 --> 00:31:06,720
held up out of sight and hearing .

419
00:31:08,000 --> 00:31:11,160
But I 've never had anything to do with the supernatural .

420
00:31:11,200 --> 00:31:14,400
Yes , you have , Eleanor . Your poltergeist experience .

421
00:31:14,680 --> 00:31:16,400
What 's a poltergeist ?

422
00:31:16,920 --> 00:31:20,280
- A playful ghost , isn 't that right , Nell ? - I wouldn 't know .

423
00:31:20,520 --> 00:31:23,400
According to the records of the International Psychic Society ...

424
00:31:23,480 --> 00:31:27,280
showers of stones fell on your house for three days when you were 10 years old .

425
00:31:27,360 --> 00:31:28,960
That 's ridiculous .

426
00:31:29,080 --> 00:31:31,000
It was witnessed by your family ...

427
00:31:31,040 --> 00:31:33,200
the neighbors , sightseers and the police .

428
00:31:33,280 --> 00:31:36,320
In fact , it 's the only case ever officially recorded by the police .

429
00:31:36,400 --> 00:31:38,000
It never happened .

430
00:31:38,760 --> 00:31:40,480
Perhaps not , if you say so .

431
00:31:40,520 --> 00:31:44,080
I only mention it because that 's the reason I wanted you in Hill House .

432
00:31:44,160 --> 00:31:45,440
Doc , level with us .

433
00:31:45,480 --> 00:31:48,160
I mean , you 're a college prof . A man with a PhD .

434
00:31:48,360 --> 00:31:51,560
You can 't really believe there 's such a thing as a haunted house .

435
00:31:51,640 --> 00:31:55,080
I wish you 'd stop referring to this desirable property as haunted .

436
00:31:55,160 --> 00:31:56,880
There 's that word " haunted " again .

437
00:31:56,960 --> 00:32:00,320
Makes me expect to find a disembodied hand in the sauce .

438
00:32:00,440 --> 00:32:03,480
Nobody knows even why some houses are called haunted .

439
00:32:03,760 --> 00:32:06,240
What would you call this place ? Fun-o-rama ?

440
00:32:07,080 --> 00:32:09,920
Diseased , sick , crazy if you like .

441
00:32:11,160 --> 00:32:14,080
A deranged house isn 't a bad way of putting it .

442
00:32:14,600 --> 00:32:17,760
Your aunt thinks that maybe Hill House was born bad .

443
00:32:18,240 --> 00:32:21,280
Such houses are described in the Bible as leprous .

444
00:32:21,360 --> 00:32:23,760
Or before that , in Homer 's phrase for the underworld :

445
00:32:23,840 --> 00:32:25,400
A house of Hades .

446
00:32:25,920 --> 00:32:27,240
Come off it , Doc .

447
00:32:27,320 --> 00:32:30,040
Really , the local mayor makes more sense to me .

448
00:32:30,320 --> 00:32:33,040
He says the disturbances are caused by subterranean waters ...

449
00:32:33,120 --> 00:32:37,240
electric currents , atmospheric pressure , sunspots , earth tremors , et cetera .

450
00:32:37,280 --> 00:32:39,960
Sure , people always want to put an easy label on things ...

451
00:32:40,000 --> 00:32:41,400
even if it 's meaningless .

452
00:32:41,440 --> 00:32:43,640
" The trouble with Hill House is sunspots . "

453
00:32:43,680 --> 00:32:46,280
There 's an explanation you don 't have to think twice about .

454
00:32:46,360 --> 00:32:48,920
And it has a scientific ring .

455
00:32:49,000 --> 00:32:51,240
That was the neighbors . They threw the rocks .

456
00:32:51,320 --> 00:32:54,480
Mother says they were against us because she wouldn 't mix with them .

457
00:32:54,560 --> 00:32:55,960
Mother says ...

458
00:32:59,520 --> 00:33:00,480
Oh , dear .

459
00:33:02,240 --> 00:33:04,160
That 's all right , Eleanor .

460
00:33:04,360 --> 00:33:06,800
- Go on . What does your mother say ? - Nothing .

461
00:33:08,400 --> 00:33:10,840
I must be more tired than I thought .

462
00:33:11,320 --> 00:33:13,440
My mother died two months ago .

463
00:33:13,760 --> 00:33:16,120
You weren 't sorry when it happened ...

464
00:33:17,080 --> 00:33:18,040
were you ?

465
00:33:18,920 --> 00:33:20,880
No , she wasn 't very happy .

466
00:33:22,160 --> 00:33:24,160
Then I won 't say I 'm sorry now .

467
00:33:24,800 --> 00:33:27,160
If I 'd known , I 'd never have asked you to come here .

468
00:33:27,200 --> 00:33:29,600
But I 'm grateful you did . I had to get away .

469
00:33:29,640 --> 00:33:32,960
- Perhaps you should ... - Please , let 's talk about something else .

470
00:33:33,200 --> 00:33:34,400
Oh , dear .

471
00:33:37,560 --> 00:33:39,680
Doc , see that ? Now what about that ?

472
00:33:39,760 --> 00:33:42,240
Does salt work against the supernatural ?

473
00:33:42,320 --> 00:33:45,960
The Montusi bushmen thought so , but they 're extinct .

474
00:33:46,720 --> 00:33:49,440
You see , you haven 't a ghost of a chance .

475
00:33:58,840 --> 00:34:00,880
I have a place in this room .

476
00:34:01,280 --> 00:34:03,320
These people are my friends .

477
00:34:03,760 --> 00:34:06,920
I 'm one of them . I belong .

478
00:34:10,200 --> 00:34:11,320
Gin !

479
00:34:11,360 --> 00:34:14,720
- That 's the fifth time , five times in a row . - $ 12 , please .

480
00:34:14,800 --> 00:34:16,920
- I hope your skirt isn 't stained . - That 's all right .

481
00:34:17,000 --> 00:34:18,720
But the upholstery on the couch .

482
00:34:18,800 --> 00:34:19,680
I 've cleanser upstairs .

483
00:34:19,760 --> 00:34:21,920
- Do you think I 'm a sucker ? - Pay up . Cash on the line .

484
00:34:22,000 --> 00:34:24,640
Over my dead body . You knew every card I had in my hand .

485
00:34:24,720 --> 00:34:27,840
- There 's a name for that . - If you mean cheating , I don 't have to .

486
00:34:27,920 --> 00:34:30,040
Okay , Miss ESP , go dream yourself up the $ 12 .

487
00:34:30,120 --> 00:34:33,040
Pay up , you welsher ! I won fair and I want my money .

488
00:34:37,520 --> 00:34:39,720
- What was it ? - I had a feeling .

489
00:34:40,360 --> 00:34:44,440
- I 'm sure it was just my imagination . - A feeling you were being watched ?

490
00:34:44,800 --> 00:34:46,040
Yes , I did .

491
00:34:46,080 --> 00:34:48,400
The house . It watches every move we make .

492
00:34:48,480 --> 00:34:51,960
- That 's your imagination . - Don 't be so cocksure of everything .

493
00:34:52,040 --> 00:34:55,640
A closed mind is the worst defense against the supernatural .

494
00:34:55,920 --> 00:34:59,960
You think you 're too civilized to need to protect yourself against evil spirits .

495
00:35:00,040 --> 00:35:04,080
But even prehistoric man had a dozen practical methods of warding them off .

496
00:35:04,160 --> 00:35:06,240
Some of your theories strike me as prehistoric .

497
00:35:06,320 --> 00:35:08,440
Besides , they downgrade property values .

498
00:35:08,520 --> 00:35:11,600
I know the supernatural is something that isn 't supposed to happen .

499
00:35:11,680 --> 00:35:13,080
Yet it does happen .

500
00:35:13,120 --> 00:35:17,120
Ghosts make the papers along with celebrities every day of the week .

501
00:35:17,440 --> 00:35:19,040
If it happens to you ...

502
00:35:19,400 --> 00:35:22,000
you 're liable to have that shut door in your mind ...

503
00:35:22,080 --> 00:35:23,640
ripped right off its hinges .

504
00:35:23,720 --> 00:35:26,760
Look , Doc , we 're buddies , but don 't try to convert me .

505
00:35:26,840 --> 00:35:28,760
I 'm trying to prepare you .

506
00:35:30,040 --> 00:35:33,520
There 's something going on in this house or I wouldn 't be here .

507
00:35:33,600 --> 00:35:34,640
What ?

508
00:35:36,680 --> 00:35:40,520
Don 't ask me to give a name to something which hasn 't got a name .

509
00:35:41,840 --> 00:35:43,280
I don 't know .

510
00:35:46,720 --> 00:35:49,480
Tomorrow we 'll see all the place . Now let 's go to bed .

511
00:35:49,560 --> 00:35:51,240
Unless anyone wants to clear out now ...

512
00:35:51,320 --> 00:35:53,440
and not have anything more to do with Hill House .

513
00:35:53,520 --> 00:35:56,280
I hope to have plenty to do with it someday , moneywise .

514
00:35:56,320 --> 00:35:58,440
We couldn 't leave now even if we wanted to .

515
00:35:58,520 --> 00:36:02,080
- You mean I 'm holding you prisoner ? - I mean Dudley keeps the gates locked .

516
00:36:02,160 --> 00:36:04,080
We could always break out .

517
00:36:04,560 --> 00:36:07,360
I have a key to the gate anytime you want it .

518
00:36:07,520 --> 00:36:10,040
- I wouldn 't dream of leaving . - Thank you .

519
00:36:10,600 --> 00:36:12,120
Adventurers all .

520
00:36:12,840 --> 00:36:15,360
But you mustn 't expect every night to be Halloween .

521
00:36:15,440 --> 00:36:17,920
Psychic phenomena are subject to certain laws .

522
00:36:18,000 --> 00:36:19,800
And just what are these laws ?

523
00:36:19,840 --> 00:36:22,280
You won 't know until you break them .

524
00:36:22,560 --> 00:36:26,360
At the end of each day , you have to fill out these forms I 've had mimeographed .

525
00:36:26,440 --> 00:36:27,960
Very scientific , aren 't we ?

526
00:36:28,040 --> 00:36:30,760
The really scientific phase won 't start for a while yet .

527
00:36:30,840 --> 00:36:33,080
First of all , we have to get orientated .

528
00:36:33,120 --> 00:36:35,400
What 's this ? Looks like " psy-kookiness . "

529
00:36:35,480 --> 00:36:37,160
Nothing like that wrong with me .

530
00:36:37,240 --> 00:36:39,320
Psychokinesis is just the technical form ...

531
00:36:39,400 --> 00:36:41,720
for what you 'd call objects moving by themselves .

532
00:36:41,800 --> 00:36:43,160
Actually , they don 't ...

533
00:36:43,200 --> 00:36:47,160
but are moved by a force from somewhere which we call psychokinesis .

534
00:36:49,400 --> 00:36:50,480
I see .

535
00:36:51,360 --> 00:36:53,560
About this ghost I can expect in my room tonight ...

536
00:36:53,640 --> 00:36:55,760
tell me , is it male or female ?

537
00:36:57,640 --> 00:36:59,520
Good night , ladies , Doc .

538
00:37:01,400 --> 00:37:04,880
I just thought of something . Nobody locked the front door .

539
00:37:05,160 --> 00:37:07,120
Won 't make any difference .

540
00:37:07,960 --> 00:37:09,000
I see .

541
00:37:11,600 --> 00:37:13,520
- Good night , Dr. Markway . - John .

542
00:37:14,240 --> 00:37:17,560
Good night , Theo . Get a good rest , Eleanor . Sleep well .

543
00:37:18,200 --> 00:37:21,880
I 'll turn the lights off below , in case you wonder who did it .

544
00:37:22,920 --> 00:37:26,000
If you feel in the least bit nervous , just run right into my room .

545
00:37:26,040 --> 00:37:27,720
Thanks . Good night .

546
00:37:28,120 --> 00:37:30,080
I 'll come in for a second .

547
00:37:30,200 --> 00:37:33,680
You 've been thinking of changing your hair . I know just the style for you .

548
00:37:33,760 --> 00:37:36,920
Why , yes . I was . But I 'm awfully tired .

549
00:37:37,480 --> 00:37:40,800
- Thanks anyhow . - Okay . We have a date for breakfast .

550
00:37:41,400 --> 00:37:42,960
Good night , Theo .

551
00:38:06,360 --> 00:38:09,320
Funny . Everything 's so ugly and yet so comfortable .

552
00:38:11,200 --> 00:38:13,040
Like drowning , I guess .

553
00:38:17,720 --> 00:38:20,440
Now I can think about them . I 'm all alone .

554
00:38:23,480 --> 00:38:24,640
Alone .

555
00:38:35,800 --> 00:38:37,760
He won 't know I locked it .

556
00:38:39,800 --> 00:38:41,440
Against what , Eleanor ?

557
00:39:10,120 --> 00:39:11,760
All right , Mother .

558
00:39:16,440 --> 00:39:18,360
Just a minute . I 'm coming .

559
00:39:26,680 --> 00:39:28,880
What , Theo ?

560
00:39:28,920 --> 00:39:30,520
Nell , in here !

561
00:39:34,280 --> 00:39:35,920
I 'm here . What is it ?

562
00:39:39,320 --> 00:39:41,360
I thought it was you pounding .

563
00:39:41,400 --> 00:39:43,680
It was . I mean , I did .

564
00:39:44,720 --> 00:39:47,760
But now it 's down near the other end of the hall .

565
00:39:50,360 --> 00:39:53,360
It 's not at all like Mother knocking on the wall .

566
00:39:53,720 --> 00:39:57,720
It 's only a noise , and the room is terribly cold .

567
00:39:58,600 --> 00:40:00,480
Terribly , terribly cold .

568
00:40:02,280 --> 00:40:04,400
It must be Luke and Dr. Markway .

569
00:40:04,680 --> 00:40:06,720
Why should they be knocking on the walls ?

570
00:40:06,800 --> 00:40:09,560
Something is . Anyway , it 's only a noise .

571
00:40:09,800 --> 00:40:11,240
Earth tremors ?

572
00:40:28,120 --> 00:40:32,080
Maybe it 'll go down on the other side of the hall .

573
00:41:04,400 --> 00:41:06,480
- No ! - Go away !

574
00:41:16,000 --> 00:41:17,520
Now I 've done it .

575
00:41:17,680 --> 00:41:20,640
It was looking for the room with someone inside .

576
00:41:27,880 --> 00:41:29,280
You big baby .

577
00:41:30,520 --> 00:41:32,840
Whatever it is , it 's just a noise .

578
00:41:32,960 --> 00:41:35,120
- I 'm cold . - So am I.

579
00:41:36,640 --> 00:41:39,000
- Where 's Luke ? Where 's Markway ? - I don 't know .

580
00:41:39,080 --> 00:41:40,600
- Warmer now ? - No .

581
00:41:41,400 --> 00:41:43,920
In a minute I 'll go out in the hall and call them .

582
00:41:44,000 --> 00:41:45,600
Are you all right ?

583
00:41:45,920 --> 00:41:47,160
Oh , God , Nell !

584
00:41:50,200 --> 00:41:52,320
It 's against the top of the door !

585
00:42:06,320 --> 00:42:07,520
It 's found us .

586
00:42:08,520 --> 00:42:12,080
Now I know why people scream , because I think I 'm going to .

587
00:42:14,440 --> 00:42:16,080
Is the door locked ?

588
00:42:55,920 --> 00:42:57,480
You can 't get in !

589
00:43:28,680 --> 00:43:29,800
It 's over .

590
00:43:31,080 --> 00:43:33,480
- How do you know ? - Can 't you feel it ?

591
00:43:33,840 --> 00:43:36,840
Aren 't you warm again ? That terrible cold has gone .

592
00:43:37,320 --> 00:43:38,480
Why , yes .

593
00:43:39,360 --> 00:43:43,120
Intense cold is one of the symptoms of shock . My mother ...

594
00:43:43,200 --> 00:43:46,080
Intense shock is one of the symptoms I 've got .

595
00:43:53,360 --> 00:43:55,080
Where have you two been ?

596
00:43:55,120 --> 00:43:57,480
What 's the matter ? You look like you 've seen a ghost .

597
00:43:57,520 --> 00:43:59,160
Did anything happen ?

598
00:44:12,240 --> 00:44:14,000
Nothing in particular ...

599
00:44:15,720 --> 00:44:18,680
just something knocked on the door with a cannonball ...

600
00:44:19,920 --> 00:44:21,640
then tried to get in and eat us .

601
00:44:21,680 --> 00:44:23,120
I 'm with Nell .

602
00:44:24,240 --> 00:44:26,960
Miss ESP and Bridey Murphy , some combination .

603
00:44:27,280 --> 00:44:30,000
- There isn 't a scratch on the wood . - Or anywhere else .

604
00:44:30,080 --> 00:44:32,480
How nice , it didn 't mar the woodwork .

605
00:44:35,320 --> 00:44:37,360
Where were you , Dr. Markway ?

606
00:44:37,720 --> 00:44:39,160
Chasing a dog .

607
00:44:39,560 --> 00:44:41,880
At least , we assumed it was a dog .

608
00:44:42,000 --> 00:44:43,840
We followed it outside .

609
00:44:46,240 --> 00:44:47,880
You mean it was inside ?

610
00:44:47,960 --> 00:44:50,280
I thought I heard something run past my room .

611
00:44:50,320 --> 00:44:53,000
I woke Luke . We went looking for it all over the house ...

612
00:44:53,040 --> 00:44:54,440
and finally out in the garden .

613
00:44:54,480 --> 00:44:57,680
But let 's face it , girls , we didn 't get very far from the house .

614
00:44:57,720 --> 00:45:00,280
Then you must 've heard that ungodly noise .

615
00:45:01,240 --> 00:45:04,080
No , there wasn 't a sound from the house .

616
00:45:04,680 --> 00:45:06,920
At least , nothing audible to us .

617
00:45:10,840 --> 00:45:13,680
- We 'd better take precautions . - Against what ?

618
00:45:14,440 --> 00:45:17,160
When Luke and I are decoyed outside ...

619
00:45:17,880 --> 00:45:20,200
and you two are bottled up inside ...

620
00:45:20,240 --> 00:45:24,200
wouldn 't you say that something , somehow , is trying to separate us ?

621
00:45:49,360 --> 00:45:51,320
Good morning , Dr. Markway .

622
00:45:51,440 --> 00:45:54,160
'Morning , and please call me John .

623
00:45:56,080 --> 00:45:59,360
- This curious life seems to agree with you . - Thank you .

624
00:45:59,520 --> 00:46:01,440
- Tea or coffee ? - Tea , please .

625
00:46:01,840 --> 00:46:03,920
How is it you look so pretty after last night ?

626
00:46:04,000 --> 00:46:05,680
That was last night .

627
00:46:05,840 --> 00:46:07,920
There may have been a little noise .

628
00:46:09,040 --> 00:46:11,640
One has to expect that in these old houses .

629
00:46:12,040 --> 00:46:14,760
I give up . I was sure you 'd be packed and on your way .

630
00:46:14,800 --> 00:46:15,760
Not likely .

631
00:46:15,840 --> 00:46:18,640
This is my first vacation in years and I 'm going to enjoy it .

632
00:46:18,720 --> 00:46:22,040
That 's the point . You need a real vacation . This isn 't the place for one .

633
00:46:22,120 --> 00:46:23,920
I mean to stay . Period .

634
00:46:24,400 --> 00:46:26,600
Unless , of course , you want to get rid of me .

635
00:46:26,680 --> 00:46:28,480
No , you mustn 't think that .

636
00:46:29,040 --> 00:46:32,000
Till last night you were just a name on my list .

637
00:46:32,080 --> 00:46:34,120
I scarcely know Eleanor Lance .

638
00:46:34,200 --> 00:46:36,680
- She 's horrible . - No , you mustn 't make fun of me .

639
00:46:36,760 --> 00:46:39,480
You 're sweet and pleasant and everyone likes you very much .

640
00:46:39,560 --> 00:46:41,680
I want to know more about you .

641
00:46:42,400 --> 00:46:45,960
I dislike lobster , crack my knuckles when I 'm nervous ...

642
00:46:47,200 --> 00:46:49,800
save buttons , and sleep on my left side .

643
00:46:50,520 --> 00:46:52,200
Why on the left side ?

644
00:46:52,280 --> 00:46:55,320
I read someplace it wears the heart out quicker .

645
00:46:56,280 --> 00:46:58,320
That 's a depressing thought .

646
00:46:59,440 --> 00:47:02,800
For the past 11 years I 've been walled up alive on a desert island .

647
00:47:02,880 --> 00:47:06,200
I thought you might be hiding some dark romantic secret in your past .

648
00:47:06,280 --> 00:47:07,480
Romantic ?

649
00:47:08,560 --> 00:47:11,960
I 've spent all my adult life taking care of my invalid mother ...

650
00:47:12,400 --> 00:47:13,880
until she died .

651
00:47:14,040 --> 00:47:15,880
No , it wasn 't romantic .

652
00:47:16,440 --> 00:47:20,240
Now that you 're free at last , you shouldn 't be wasting your time in Hill House .

653
00:47:20,320 --> 00:47:22,640
- It 's a mistake . - But it isn 't , don 't you see ?

654
00:47:22,720 --> 00:47:24,840
The only thing that kept me going ...

655
00:47:25,200 --> 00:47:27,280
was that someday I knew something would happen .

656
00:47:27,360 --> 00:47:30,640
Something truly extraordinary , like Hill House .

657
00:47:31,840 --> 00:47:33,720
Yes , it 's extraordinary .

658
00:47:34,480 --> 00:47:36,720
What 'll you do when you get back ? Do you have a job ?

659
00:47:36,800 --> 00:47:39,880
No job , nothing . I don 't know what I 'm going to do .

660
00:47:41,360 --> 00:47:43,680
You wouldn 't send me back , would you ?

661
00:47:43,760 --> 00:47:45,640
That depends on what happens .

662
00:47:46,560 --> 00:47:48,560
We may all have to go back .

663
00:47:48,680 --> 00:47:50,080
But I won 't give up easily .

664
00:47:50,160 --> 00:47:53,240
How did you get so interested in the supernatural ?

665
00:47:53,720 --> 00:47:57,480
I didn 't want to become what my father called a practical man .

666
00:47:58,160 --> 00:48:01,280
I come from one of those respectable English families ...

667
00:48:01,360 --> 00:48:04,160
that dragged all the Victorian virtues into the 20th century .

668
00:48:04,240 --> 00:48:06,120
In a Gladstone bag , of course .

669
00:48:06,160 --> 00:48:08,640
Everything had to be practical and conventional .

670
00:48:08,720 --> 00:48:10,240
So my first reaction as a kid ...

671
00:48:10,320 --> 00:48:13,200
was to choose something useless and unconventional . Like ghosts .

672
00:48:13,280 --> 00:48:15,320
But you 're an anthropologist now .

673
00:48:15,680 --> 00:48:18,600
When I refused to read law at Oxford as my father had ...

674
00:48:18,680 --> 00:48:20,360
there was a terrific row .

675
00:48:20,520 --> 00:48:23,200
I took off for America , without my Gladstone bag ...

676
00:48:23,280 --> 00:48:25,160
and worked my way through college .

677
00:48:25,200 --> 00:48:27,240
I decided on anthropology because it seemed ...

678
00:48:27,320 --> 00:48:29,560
to be a short step from the study of dead souls ...

679
00:48:29,640 --> 00:48:32,600
to the study of dead men and dead civilizations .

680
00:48:32,680 --> 00:48:34,560
I 'm not very practical , either .

681
00:48:34,960 --> 00:48:37,280
But it didn 't occur to me till I was hooked ...

682
00:48:37,360 --> 00:48:40,480
that my combined knowledge of anthropology and psychic phenomena ...

683
00:48:40,560 --> 00:48:42,920
had led me on to something very practical .

684
00:48:43,120 --> 00:48:46,400
You see , if ghosts , which are pure spirit , come from man ...

685
00:48:46,480 --> 00:48:49,600
then perhaps it 's possible some day to have individuals ...

686
00:48:49,800 --> 00:48:53,920
whose spiritual caliber far surpasses anything humanity has yet known .

687
00:48:54,240 --> 00:48:56,800
Human nature could certainly stand some improvements .

688
00:48:56,880 --> 00:48:59,480
However , my idea remains pure theory ...

689
00:48:59,560 --> 00:49:02,760
until somebody proves definitely the supernatural exists .

690
00:49:03,560 --> 00:49:06,760
Anyway , that 's enough about me . Now tell me about last night .

691
00:49:07,240 --> 00:49:08,320
Thank you .

692
00:49:08,360 --> 00:49:10,560
I 've been trying to remember .

693
00:49:10,640 --> 00:49:13,240
I can remember knowing I was frightened ...

694
00:49:13,560 --> 00:49:17,120
but I can 't remember actually being frightened , or how I felt .

695
00:49:17,440 --> 00:49:19,360
I think it 's because it was so unreal .

696
00:49:19,440 --> 00:49:22,200
Still could be subterranean waters , you know .

697
00:49:22,280 --> 00:49:25,240
I hope not . That wouldn 't be nearly so exciting .

698
00:49:25,720 --> 00:49:28,200
Not good , this feeling of excitement .

699
00:49:28,720 --> 00:49:32,480
It 's the first sign you 've fallen under the spell of the house .

700
00:49:32,840 --> 00:49:34,960
Maybe it isn 't just the house .

701
00:49:35,480 --> 00:49:36,960
Then what else ?

702
00:49:39,520 --> 00:49:41,520
Let 's blame it on sunspots .

703
00:49:42,760 --> 00:49:45,000
Well , it wasn 't sunspots last night .

704
00:49:45,640 --> 00:49:49,120
If anyone gets hurt , it 's going to be your fault , Markway .

705
00:49:49,720 --> 00:49:53,520
No ghost in all the long history of ghosts ever hurt anyone physically .

706
00:49:53,600 --> 00:49:56,640
We weren 't in any actual danger at all , isn 't that right , John ?

707
00:49:56,720 --> 00:49:57,960
No , not entirely .

708
00:49:58,040 --> 00:50:00,200
Fear alone can do the damage to the victim .

709
00:50:00,240 --> 00:50:03,360
Prehistoric man , for instance , could die of fright during an eclipse .

710
00:50:03,400 --> 00:50:06,040
- Poor sap . - You mean poor homo sapiens .

711
00:50:07,400 --> 00:50:10,440
A modern man can react with the same unreasoning terror ...

712
00:50:10,520 --> 00:50:11,880
to a supernatural event .

713
00:50:11,920 --> 00:50:14,680
Especially if he doesn 't believe that the supernatural exists .

714
00:50:14,760 --> 00:50:17,920
I 've always been more afraid of being left alone or left out ...

715
00:50:17,960 --> 00:50:20,480
than of things that go bump in the night .

716
00:50:21,320 --> 00:50:23,200
What are you afraid of , Theo ?

717
00:50:23,560 --> 00:50:25,720
Of knowing what I really want .

718
00:50:27,400 --> 00:50:30,800
- Good morning , fellow earthlings . - Luke , what are you afraid of ?

719
00:50:30,880 --> 00:50:32,920
What I just saw in the hall .

720
00:50:33,240 --> 00:50:36,160
- Is there something ? - You mean you haven 't seen it ?

721
00:50:37,160 --> 00:50:39,520
The show 's just getting good . Come on .

722
00:50:45,040 --> 00:50:46,120
Right here .

723
00:50:48,720 --> 00:50:50,120
It 's writing ?

724
00:50:50,560 --> 00:50:51,680
Writing .

725
00:50:54,800 --> 00:50:55,920
Chalk .

726
00:50:58,440 --> 00:51:00,080
Or something like chalk .

727
00:51:09,960 --> 00:51:11,680
- Can you read it ? - No .

728
00:51:19,880 --> 00:51:20,960
What ?

729
00:51:23,560 --> 00:51:24,800
No .

730
00:51:25,280 --> 00:51:28,240
Wipe it off , please . It 's crazy .

731
00:51:28,680 --> 00:51:30,600
Crazy is the word for it , all right .

732
00:51:30,640 --> 00:51:33,760
- Get something and wipe it off , Luke . - But it 's crazy . Why ?

733
00:51:33,840 --> 00:51:36,360
Why all the fuss ? It spelled her name right , didn 't it ?

734
00:51:36,440 --> 00:51:38,600
- Those letters spelled out my name . - Take it easy .

735
00:51:38,680 --> 00:51:42,080
It 's my name ! It belongs to me and something is using it .

736
00:51:42,120 --> 00:51:44,080
Writing it and calling me with my own name !

737
00:51:44,160 --> 00:51:46,160
- Just because your name ... - That 's it !

738
00:51:46,240 --> 00:51:48,320
It knows my name , doesn 't it ?

739
00:51:48,480 --> 00:51:50,760
- It knows my name ! - Simmer down , Nell .

740
00:51:50,840 --> 00:51:53,320
It could have said any of us . It knows all our names .

741
00:51:53,400 --> 00:51:56,480
Did you write it ? Please tell me . I won 't be angry or anything .

742
00:51:56,520 --> 00:51:58,720
I just want to know so that ...

743
00:51:58,760 --> 00:52:01,280
Maybe it was only for a joke to frighten me .

744
00:52:01,720 --> 00:52:03,840
You know none of us wrote it , baby .

745
00:52:03,880 --> 00:52:06,080
- She 's lying , I could swear she did it . - Easy .

746
00:52:06,160 --> 00:52:07,840
I clear breakfast at 10 : 00 .

747
00:52:07,880 --> 00:52:10,360
- Why should I write your name ? - I set lunch at 1 : 00 .

748
00:52:10,440 --> 00:52:12,400
Because I didn 't wait to have breakfast with you .

749
00:52:12,480 --> 00:52:15,000
- You 're way out . - You don 't know Theo as I 'm beginning to .

750
00:52:15,080 --> 00:52:17,520
- I clear up at 10 : 00 . - Mrs. Dudley , please !

751
00:52:17,800 --> 00:52:20,400
- No one blames you for being upset . - It 's 10 : 00 .

752
00:52:20,480 --> 00:52:22,720
Why me ? Why should I be the one chosen ?

753
00:52:22,800 --> 00:52:25,200
Maybe something in the house finds you a kindred spirit .

754
00:52:25,280 --> 00:52:28,800
Maybe it thinks you have more understanding and sympathy than we do .

755
00:52:29,280 --> 00:52:31,000
Maybe you wrote it yourself .

756
00:52:31,080 --> 00:52:33,440
Sure , I 'm just the kind to want to see my name ...

757
00:52:33,480 --> 00:52:37,200
- scribbled all over this foul house ! - It 's one way to attract attention , isn 't it ?

758
00:52:37,280 --> 00:52:39,840
You think I like the idea I 'm the center of attention ?

759
00:52:39,920 --> 00:52:42,800
Why are you all done up in that new hairstyle ?

760
00:52:46,120 --> 00:52:48,480
- You were the one who suggested ... - That 's enough .

761
00:52:48,520 --> 00:52:50,040
How dare you ?

762
00:52:50,120 --> 00:52:52,840
Can 't you see Theo 's just trying to get a rise out of you ...

763
00:52:52,920 --> 00:52:55,320
so you won 't be frightened anymore ?

764
00:52:57,800 --> 00:52:59,080
I 'm sorry .

765
00:52:59,480 --> 00:53:01,120
Take Eleanor to her room .

766
00:53:01,520 --> 00:53:03,440
We 'll postpone the tour of the house .

767
00:53:03,520 --> 00:53:06,840
Okay , but don 't forget . I don 't want to spend another night ...

768
00:53:06,920 --> 00:53:09,480
wondering what 's over my head or underneath me .

769
00:53:11,840 --> 00:53:14,120
You wouldn 't leave me behind , would you ?

770
00:53:14,440 --> 00:53:16,280
No one will leave you behind .

771
00:53:28,400 --> 00:53:29,760
Holy cow ! Mount Rushmore !

772
00:53:29,840 --> 00:53:32,840
- It 's not there . I don 't believe it 's there . - How ?

773
00:53:33,480 --> 00:53:35,160
I thought you 'd get a kick out of it .

774
00:53:35,240 --> 00:53:37,960
It 's supposed to be St. Francis curing the lepers .

775
00:53:38,440 --> 00:53:40,360
I 'd say it 's a family portrait .

776
00:53:40,520 --> 00:53:41,640
A composite .

777
00:53:41,960 --> 00:53:44,520
The tall , draped , masculine type ...

778
00:53:44,600 --> 00:53:46,680
that 's old Hugh Crain ...

779
00:53:46,760 --> 00:53:50,200
pointing out all the great treasures in this creepy house he built .

780
00:53:50,280 --> 00:53:53,600
The dame on the end down there and this one must be his two wives .

781
00:53:53,680 --> 00:53:55,520
His daughter , Abigail .

782
00:53:56,120 --> 00:53:58,880
- Now the dog ... - The dog you were chasing last night .

783
00:53:59,240 --> 00:54:00,880
Yeah , very good .

784
00:54:01,920 --> 00:54:04,520
Now that one , she 's got to be the companion .

785
00:54:04,680 --> 00:54:07,240
The one who 's supposed to have murdered Abigail .

786
00:54:07,320 --> 00:54:10,200
No , that was much later . When Abigail was an old lady .

787
00:54:11,040 --> 00:54:14,520
I wonder how this statue got here . It wasn 't on the original inventory .

788
00:54:14,600 --> 00:54:16,640
Maybe I 'll break it up and sell it for tombstones .

789
00:54:16,720 --> 00:54:18,720
The companion reminds me of you , Nell .

790
00:54:18,800 --> 00:54:20,160
Oh , no !

791
00:54:20,400 --> 00:54:21,720
She does at that .

792
00:54:22,440 --> 00:54:24,320
A natural beauty , I 'd call her .

793
00:54:26,320 --> 00:54:28,320
What does he think of me , really ?

794
00:54:28,800 --> 00:54:30,120
Am I being a fool ?

795
00:54:31,160 --> 00:54:34,200
Don 't let me know too surely what he thinks of me .

796
00:54:34,600 --> 00:54:36,800
This could be a family portrait of us .

797
00:54:36,880 --> 00:54:39,680
- Don 't be ridiculous . - You 're the companion .

798
00:54:40,120 --> 00:54:42,360
I 'm Abigail , grown up .

799
00:54:42,880 --> 00:54:44,720
And Markway could be old Hugh .

800
00:54:44,960 --> 00:54:47,040
- Where do I fit in ? - The dog .

801
00:54:48,840 --> 00:54:50,920
When are you going to show me your ESP ?

802
00:54:51,000 --> 00:54:52,640
Keep your hands to yourself .

803
00:54:52,680 --> 00:54:54,200
What 's going on ?

804
00:54:55,400 --> 00:54:57,040
More than meets the eye .

805
00:54:58,080 --> 00:55:01,960
You know , this wouldn 't be such a bad room without the statue .

806
00:55:02,400 --> 00:55:04,680
Ideal for the zombies ' annual ball .

807
00:55:06,880 --> 00:55:09,720
Why don 't you dance with Hugh ? I believe he has his eye on you .

808
00:55:09,800 --> 00:55:11,280
- That 's not funny . - Don 't be chicken .

809
00:55:11,360 --> 00:55:13,920
- Leave her alone . - I bet she doesn 't know how to dance .

810
00:55:13,960 --> 00:55:15,200
I do , too .

811
00:55:19,040 --> 00:55:21,480
Hugh Crain , will you dance with me ?

812
00:55:22,720 --> 00:55:24,640
I believe he 's going to accept .

813
00:55:38,000 --> 00:55:39,880
- He moved . - Of course .

814
00:55:39,960 --> 00:55:43,040
Haven 't you noticed how nothing in the house moves till you look away ...

815
00:55:43,080 --> 00:55:46,720
and then you just catch something out of the corner of your eye ?

816
00:55:48,920 --> 00:55:50,400
She stepped on my toe .

817
00:55:51,520 --> 00:55:54,280
Let 's go out this way before somebody gets hurt .

818
00:55:58,000 --> 00:56:01,280
Come over here , I want to show you something really unique .

819
00:56:10,080 --> 00:56:12,400
A library complete with ivory tower .

820
00:56:14,400 --> 00:56:15,920
I can 't go in there .

821
00:56:17,600 --> 00:56:19,360
- My mother ... - Yes ?

822
00:56:20,280 --> 00:56:21,440
That smell ...

823
00:56:23,600 --> 00:56:27,080
- It 's just stale air , Eleanor . - No , that other smell ... Awful .

824
00:56:28,200 --> 00:56:29,920
Smells sweet to me , honey .

825
00:56:30,080 --> 00:56:33,480
At 25 cents a book , I should do all right with this room .

826
00:56:33,560 --> 00:56:36,800
I don 't think I 'll do much reading while I 'm here .

827
00:56:37,080 --> 00:56:40,320
- Not if the books smell like the library . - I didn 't notice it .

828
00:56:40,920 --> 00:56:43,520
No , that 's good , Eleanor . It 's just what we 're after .

829
00:56:43,600 --> 00:56:46,200
Try and remember your reaction and describe it exactly ...

830
00:56:46,280 --> 00:56:49,080
- when you write your notes tonight . - That 's what I 'm here for .

831
00:56:49,120 --> 00:56:52,120
Only , do you mind if I skip the library for now ?

832
00:56:52,160 --> 00:56:55,120
No , do just what you want . We 'll only be a minute .

833
00:56:57,760 --> 00:56:59,800
- You 're sure you 're all right ? - Yes .

834
00:57:06,040 --> 00:57:08,280
I want to show you something really interesting .

835
00:57:08,320 --> 00:57:11,040
You remember that companion , the one that Abigail had ...

836
00:57:11,080 --> 00:57:13,840
when she was an old lady ? See that little balcony ...

837
00:57:14,880 --> 00:57:17,880
clear up at the top there , right up there in the shadows ?

838
00:57:19,040 --> 00:57:20,880
That 's where the companion hanged herself .

839
00:57:20,960 --> 00:57:23,480
- It would have been easier to jump . - Without a parachute ?

840
00:57:23,520 --> 00:57:25,920
They say she tied the rope on to the railing and then ...

841
00:57:26,000 --> 00:57:27,600
Thanks , we get it .

842
00:57:27,800 --> 00:57:29,240
I just had a great idea .

843
00:57:29,280 --> 00:57:33,000
You know what I 'll do with this room ? After I inherit the house , of course .

844
00:57:33,080 --> 00:57:34,720
I 'll turn it into a nightclub .

845
00:57:34,800 --> 00:57:37,560
Tear out these bookshelves and put a band in there .

846
00:57:38,640 --> 00:57:39,880
Now comes the best part .

847
00:57:39,960 --> 00:57:42,680
A line of beautiful chorus girls dancing down these stairs .

848
00:57:42,720 --> 00:57:44,040
Can 't you see it ?

849
00:57:48,760 --> 00:57:50,720
- Are you all right ? - I think so .

850
00:57:50,800 --> 00:57:52,320
- Quick thinking . - Instinct .

851
00:57:52,400 --> 00:57:54,960
My strong instinct for self-preservation .

852
00:57:55,040 --> 00:57:58,840
And it 's telling me right now loud and clear to get the hell out of here .

853
00:58:08,280 --> 00:58:10,000
Vile . Hideous .

854
00:58:21,080 --> 00:58:24,040
I wonder what it would be like looking down from there .

855
00:58:24,840 --> 00:58:26,640
That 's where she did it .

856
00:58:27,320 --> 00:58:28,640
From that window .

857
00:58:29,440 --> 00:58:31,640
Climbing out through the bars ...

858
00:58:32,480 --> 00:58:36,440
hanging on for an instant , hanging on ...

859
00:58:42,080 --> 00:58:43,800
Eleanor , you 'll fall !

860
00:58:44,640 --> 00:58:46,360
Didn 't you hear me calling ?

861
00:58:46,800 --> 00:58:50,040
This house , you have to watch it every minute .

862
00:58:54,120 --> 00:58:57,760
I didn 't realize you were so nervous . I think I should send you home .

863
00:58:57,840 --> 00:59:00,960
- No , please , I can 't go home . - It 's no reflection on you .

864
00:59:01,040 --> 00:59:03,120
An atmosphere like this might break anyone down .

865
00:59:03,200 --> 00:59:04,920
But I 'm not breaking down .

866
00:59:05,240 --> 00:59:06,800
I did hear noises last night .

867
00:59:06,880 --> 00:59:09,240
Something was trying to get into the room .

868
00:59:12,280 --> 00:59:16,960
You realize that if even one event is proved to be a hallucination ...

869
00:59:17,720 --> 00:59:20,240
then this whole experiment will be questioned .

870
00:59:21,120 --> 00:59:23,280
I 'm not crazy , you know .

871
00:59:23,560 --> 00:59:27,520
After all , Theo was there , too . Is it my fault it just didn 't make sense ?

872
00:59:32,880 --> 00:59:34,680
We 'll let it go for now .

873
00:59:35,880 --> 00:59:38,480
- Maybe I 'm just being selfish . - Selfish ?

874
00:59:38,680 --> 00:59:41,280
Keeping you here for the sake of the experiment .

875
00:59:41,920 --> 00:59:44,760
Of course , for the sake of the experiment .

876
00:59:44,800 --> 00:59:47,120
You do seem to be the main attraction ...

877
00:59:48,120 --> 00:59:49,880
for whatever 's in the house .

878
00:59:50,080 --> 00:59:54,000
- But I 'll send you back the minute ... - No , please . I 'm all right . Really I am .

879
00:59:57,280 --> 00:59:59,360
Well , don 't you two look cozy .

880
01:00:01,040 --> 01:00:03,800
She was halfway off the verandah when I caught her .

881
01:00:04,360 --> 01:00:07,320
I was leaning back to see the top of the tower .

882
01:00:07,800 --> 01:00:10,200
- I got dizzy . - Dizzy like a fox ?

883
01:00:12,320 --> 01:00:13,440
Poor Nell .

884
01:00:13,720 --> 01:00:16,680
You look like death . Let 's go inside .

885
01:00:22,280 --> 01:00:24,640
I think you 'd better move in with Eleanor .

886
01:00:24,720 --> 01:00:27,960
- You 're the doctor . - But that 's my room , my very own room .

887
01:00:28,160 --> 01:00:31,800
I wouldn 't want to risk either of you spending another night alone .

888
01:00:32,560 --> 01:00:34,320
Don 't get all hung up , Nell .

889
01:00:34,880 --> 01:00:37,840
We 'll have fun . Like sisters .

890
01:00:46,160 --> 01:00:48,080
- It tickles . - Of course .

891
01:00:48,800 --> 01:00:50,520
Your toes are tickled pink .

892
01:00:50,720 --> 01:00:53,080
I knew my shade would suit you perfectly .

893
01:00:54,080 --> 01:00:56,440
Have another drink . It will keep the chill out .

894
01:00:56,520 --> 01:00:58,840
Just a teensy one . To keep the chill out .

895
01:01:00,000 --> 01:01:02,520
- I don 't really like whisky . - This is brandy .

896
01:01:04,400 --> 01:01:08,000
By the time I 'm through with you , Nell , you 'll be a different person .

897
01:01:10,040 --> 01:01:11,320
It 's wicked .

898
01:01:12,200 --> 01:01:13,600
I mean , on my foot .

899
01:01:13,920 --> 01:01:16,520
You 've got foolishness and wickedness mixed up .

900
01:01:17,400 --> 01:01:18,720
Maybe .

901
01:01:19,120 --> 01:01:21,720
Haven 't had much chance to learn the difference .

902
01:01:22,440 --> 01:01:25,360
Know something ? Even when I 'd play solitaire in my room ...

903
01:01:25,440 --> 01:01:27,680
she 'd bang on the wall and make me feel guilty ...

904
01:01:27,760 --> 01:01:30,040
for leaving her alone just that little bit .

905
01:01:30,120 --> 01:01:32,160
- She 'd always ... - Your mother ?

906
01:01:33,880 --> 01:01:36,200
My mother ...

907
01:01:39,080 --> 01:01:40,840
Story of my dull life .

908
01:01:42,680 --> 01:01:44,440
What 's your apartment like ?

909
01:01:44,680 --> 01:01:48,680
It 's an old place we furnished ourselves from stuff we picked up in the junk shops .

910
01:01:48,760 --> 01:01:50,840
We both love fixing over old things .

911
01:01:51,080 --> 01:01:52,200
Like me .

912
01:01:55,320 --> 01:01:56,400
You married ?

913
01:01:57,560 --> 01:01:58,480
No .

914
01:02:00,280 --> 01:02:01,480
I 'm sorry .

915
01:02:03,280 --> 01:02:06,120
I 'm stupid and wicked and untrustworthy ...

916
01:02:06,200 --> 01:02:08,920
- and not good for anything at all . - I don 't think so .

917
01:02:09,000 --> 01:02:11,400
Maybe just a little tight at the moment .

918
01:02:12,040 --> 01:02:14,320
Tell me something about where you live .

919
01:02:18,120 --> 01:02:21,280
I haven 't had it long enough to believe it 's my own .

920
01:02:21,640 --> 01:02:25,200
It 's a little apartment . Smaller than yours , I 'm sure .

921
01:02:25,880 --> 01:02:28,400
I live alone . I 'm still furnishing it .

922
01:02:29,280 --> 01:02:33,200
Buying one thing at a time to make sure I get everything right .

923
01:02:35,080 --> 01:02:39,240
Took me two weeks to find the little stone lions I keep on the mantel .

924
01:02:40,560 --> 01:02:42,400
Brush their teeth every night .

925
01:02:43,240 --> 01:02:46,800
I 've got a hunch I better get you back to your apartment as fast as I can .

926
01:02:46,880 --> 01:02:48,480
- Don 't say that . - I only mean ...

927
01:02:48,560 --> 01:02:50,080
Why do you all pick on me ?

928
01:02:50,160 --> 01:02:53,160
Am I the public dump or something for everybody 's fear ?

929
01:02:56,720 --> 01:02:59,360
I don 't want to leave Hill House ever .

930
01:03:02,360 --> 01:03:05,720
I 've been waiting all my life for something like this to happen .

931
01:03:07,480 --> 01:03:09,760
Hey , everybody , come here . I 've found something .

932
01:03:16,200 --> 01:03:17,760
What 's wrong with you , Doc ?

933
01:03:17,840 --> 01:03:21,640
Stand there , go on . You , too , girls . Stand there .

934
01:03:25,280 --> 01:03:27,680
A genuine cold spot .

935
01:03:27,800 --> 01:03:30,400
I guarantee it won 't register on any thermometer .

936
01:03:30,480 --> 01:03:33,040
Bunk . It 's just a draft , that 's all .

937
01:03:33,720 --> 01:03:36,440
- Coming from somewhere . - A draft ? In Hill House ?

938
01:03:36,520 --> 01:03:38,960
Not unless you can make one of the doors stay open .

939
01:03:39,040 --> 01:03:42,560
No , I found it . The heart of Hill House .

940
01:03:43,000 --> 01:03:44,880
You mean where we 're standing ?

941
01:03:45,400 --> 01:03:46,840
Behind these doors .

942
01:03:47,640 --> 01:03:49,480
- What 's in there ? - The nursery .

943
01:03:49,880 --> 01:03:52,520
Abigail Crain grew up and died there .

944
01:03:54,040 --> 01:03:57,160
- Just the place to chill our beer . - No , don 't go in there .

945
01:03:57,480 --> 01:04:01,360
We 'll keep the lid on the pressure cooker a while longer , then .

946
01:04:01,560 --> 01:04:03,320
Now don 't give me that , Doc .

947
01:04:03,440 --> 01:04:05,840
It 's like the doorway to a tomb .

948
01:04:06,520 --> 01:04:07,800
Bless you .

949
01:04:09,040 --> 01:04:10,720
Now , that 's enough , girls .

950
01:04:10,800 --> 01:04:13,080
You 'd better run along to bed before you catch cold .

951
01:04:13,160 --> 01:04:15,080
Yes , teacher . Bless you .

952
01:04:15,560 --> 01:04:16,520
Come on .

953
01:04:29,560 --> 01:04:31,520
No . There 's got to be a draft .

954
01:04:33,760 --> 01:04:35,360
The floor 's solid .

955
01:04:35,880 --> 01:04:38,640
Look , Doc , don 't give me any of that supernatural jazz .

956
01:04:38,680 --> 01:04:42,680
This is something I can feel . And see .

957
01:04:43,160 --> 01:04:45,880
Maybe there 's a pipeline to the North Pole .

958
01:04:46,200 --> 01:04:50,000
Why won 't you accept it for what it is : A supernatural phenomenon ?

959
01:04:50,160 --> 01:04:52,240
You knock on wood , don 't you ?

960
01:04:52,640 --> 01:04:55,080
Yeah , what 's that got to do with it ?

961
01:04:55,360 --> 01:04:57,720
It shows that even you , despite yourself ...

962
01:04:57,800 --> 01:05:01,680
feel that there are forces beyond nature able to help or hurt us .

963
01:05:02,680 --> 01:05:03,600
Wait a minute .

964
01:05:03,680 --> 01:05:06,040
Are you telling me that belief in a superstition ...

965
01:05:06,120 --> 01:05:08,720
is the same thing as believing in the supernatural ?

966
01:05:08,760 --> 01:05:10,280
It 's food for thought .

967
01:05:14,080 --> 01:05:15,720
Frozen food for thought .

968
01:05:22,440 --> 01:05:23,760
You know what I think ?

969
01:05:23,800 --> 01:05:26,600
Markway has us all so edgy , we 're getting the cold sweats .

970
01:05:26,680 --> 01:05:29,200
The temperature needn 't drop to make you feel like that .

971
01:05:29,240 --> 01:05:30,680
That 's right .

972
01:05:30,760 --> 01:05:32,680
Music gives me goose bumps .

973
01:05:33,320 --> 01:05:35,560
Still , there was that awful smell in the library .

974
01:05:35,640 --> 01:05:37,440
Here we go again . You know very well ...

975
01:05:37,520 --> 01:05:40,880
what you thought you smelled in the library . The sickroom smell .

976
01:05:41,760 --> 01:05:44,080
Let 's discuss me some other time .

977
01:05:44,760 --> 01:05:46,000
I 'm tired .

978
01:05:46,680 --> 01:05:49,360
- Turn out the light . - I 'd like it on . Have you seen this ?

979
01:05:49,400 --> 01:05:52,600
I told you . I just want to go to sleep . Good night !

980
01:05:54,520 --> 01:05:57,800
Why be mad at me ? I don 't think you killed your mother .

981
01:06:02,600 --> 01:06:03,840
Leave me alone .

982
01:06:05,320 --> 01:06:06,400
Go to sleep !

983
01:06:06,840 --> 01:06:08,480
Good night , Nellie my Nell .

984
01:07:05,440 --> 01:07:08,400
Are you awake ? Don 't say a word , Theo . Not a word .

985
01:07:08,920 --> 01:07:11,000
Don 't let it know you 're in my room .

986
01:07:32,720 --> 01:07:34,120
Hold my hand .

987
01:07:37,160 --> 01:07:38,960
And for God 's sake , don 't scream .

988
01:08:04,440 --> 01:08:07,240
Is it over ? Do you think it 's over ?

989
01:08:09,040 --> 01:08:10,640
You 're breaking my hand .

990
01:08:30,680 --> 01:08:32,680
This is monstrous . This is cruel .

991
01:08:32,880 --> 01:08:36,280
It is hurting a child and I will not let anyone ...

992
01:08:36,360 --> 01:08:37,960
anything hurt a child .

993
01:08:38,560 --> 01:08:41,280
I won 't endure this . It thinks to scare me .

994
01:08:41,360 --> 01:08:43,200
It has , and poor Theo , too .

995
01:08:43,600 --> 01:08:46,840
Honestly , it feels like she 's breaking my hand .

996
01:08:55,000 --> 01:08:57,640
I will take a lot from this filthy house for his sake ...

997
01:08:57,680 --> 01:09:01,120
but I will not go along with hurting a child . No , I will not .

998
01:09:01,480 --> 01:09:05,880
I will get my mouth to open right now , and I will yell .

999
01:09:08,080 --> 01:09:09,760
Stop it !

1000
01:09:16,560 --> 01:09:18,120
What , Nell ?

1001
01:09:23,920 --> 01:09:24,840
Oh , God !

1002
01:09:30,280 --> 01:09:31,920
Whose hand was I holding ?

1003
01:09:59,440 --> 01:10:02,440
- Eleanor , too bad . You just missed it . - What ?

1004
01:10:02,880 --> 01:10:05,120
The Hill House Concerto for Harp .

1005
01:10:06,480 --> 01:10:08,160
Were you playing the harp ?

1006
01:10:08,360 --> 01:10:09,880
It was playing itself .

1007
01:10:11,000 --> 01:10:13,200
Naturally . How do you explain it ?

1008
01:10:13,680 --> 01:10:15,760
Subterranean waters ? Earth tremors ?

1009
01:10:15,960 --> 01:10:19,600
As a matter of fact , I don 't think it is anything supernatural .

1010
01:10:19,800 --> 01:10:21,440
The self-starting music .

1011
01:10:21,600 --> 01:10:24,400
More likely it 's in the realm of the preternatural .

1012
01:10:24,480 --> 01:10:27,400
Something we don 't have any natural explanation for right now ...

1013
01:10:27,480 --> 01:10:29,600
but probably will have some day .

1014
01:10:29,680 --> 01:10:33,440
The preternatural of one generation becomes the natural of the next .

1015
01:10:34,680 --> 01:10:38,400
Not so long ago , scientists laughed at the idea of magnetic attraction .

1016
01:10:38,920 --> 01:10:42,440
They couldn 't explain it , so they refused to admit it existed .

1017
01:10:42,920 --> 01:10:45,320
Life is still full of the preternatural .

1018
01:10:45,880 --> 01:10:47,080
My mother ...

1019
01:10:47,560 --> 01:10:50,120
Go on . Say it . You 've been trying to since you got here .

1020
01:10:50,200 --> 01:10:53,720
I don 't know what I was going to say . I 'm still so terrified from last night .

1021
01:10:53,800 --> 01:10:56,200
You shouldn 't be . It 's silly to be frightened .

1022
01:10:56,280 --> 01:10:58,040
You haven 't been through it .

1023
01:10:58,800 --> 01:11:00,760
This horrible unknown thing .

1024
01:11:00,920 --> 01:11:03,240
Unknown . That 's the key word .

1025
01:11:03,880 --> 01:11:05,800
When we get involved in a supernatural event ...

1026
01:11:05,880 --> 01:11:08,800
we 're scared out of our wits just because it 's unknown .

1027
01:11:08,880 --> 01:11:10,600
The night cry of a child .

1028
01:11:10,840 --> 01:11:12,800
Face on the wall , knockings , bangings .

1029
01:11:12,880 --> 01:11:14,040
What 's there to be afraid of ?

1030
01:11:14,120 --> 01:11:17,400
You weren 't threatened . It was harmless , like a joke that didn 't come off .

1031
01:11:17,480 --> 01:11:19,240
- But the child ... - There was no child .

1032
01:11:19,320 --> 01:11:20,880
- Just a voice . - Worse .

1033
01:11:22,200 --> 01:11:24,040
Look , let me put it this way .

1034
01:11:24,840 --> 01:11:27,160
When people believed the Earth was flat ...

1035
01:11:27,240 --> 01:11:29,880
the idea of a round world scared them silly .

1036
01:11:30,000 --> 01:11:32,520
Then they found out how the round world works .

1037
01:11:32,560 --> 01:11:35,080
It 's the same with the world of the supernatural .

1038
01:11:35,120 --> 01:11:36,960
Until we know how it works ...

1039
01:11:37,440 --> 01:11:41,040
we 'll continue to carry around this unnecessary burden of fear .

1040
01:11:44,560 --> 01:11:47,080
Supposing it is in my imagination ...

1041
01:11:47,720 --> 01:11:50,360
the knocking , the voices , everything .

1042
01:11:52,560 --> 01:11:54,560
Every cursed bit of the haunting .

1043
01:11:57,240 --> 01:11:59,560
Suppose the haunting is all in my mind .

1044
01:11:59,640 --> 01:12:02,640
You can 't say that because there are three other people here .

1045
01:12:02,720 --> 01:12:04,960
We all resist the idea ...

1046
01:12:05,160 --> 01:12:08,240
that what ran through the garden the first night was a ghost ...

1047
01:12:08,320 --> 01:12:11,920
what banged on the door was a ghost , what held your hand was a ghost .

1048
01:12:12,040 --> 01:12:14,760
But there 's certainly something going on in Hill House .

1049
01:12:14,840 --> 01:12:18,360
We 're getting close , Eleanor , very close to finding out what it is .

1050
01:12:18,520 --> 01:12:21,960
I could say all three of you are in my imagination . None of this is real .

1051
01:12:22,040 --> 01:12:24,680
Sure . That 's the easiest way to dismiss the supernatural ...

1052
01:12:24,720 --> 01:12:27,440
by pleading insanity or accusing others of it .

1053
01:12:27,600 --> 01:12:29,040
Maybe I am insane .

1054
01:12:34,320 --> 01:12:36,040
The night my mother died ...

1055
01:12:37,040 --> 01:12:38,640
she knocked on the wall .

1056
01:12:39,560 --> 01:12:40,880
And I didn 't come .

1057
01:12:43,120 --> 01:12:46,200
Eleven years of looking in on her after every small noise .

1058
01:12:46,960 --> 01:12:48,160
That night ...

1059
01:12:49,440 --> 01:12:51,080
my back hurt and my hands .

1060
01:12:51,640 --> 01:12:54,440
It wasn 't fair . We could 've afforded a laundress .

1061
01:12:54,720 --> 01:12:57,960
I ought to have brought her the medicine . I always did before .

1062
01:12:58,120 --> 01:12:59,280
This time ...

1063
01:13:01,200 --> 01:13:02,480
she called me ...

1064
01:13:03,360 --> 01:13:04,880
and I never answered .

1065
01:13:07,640 --> 01:13:09,960
- Is that how a normal person acts ? - Yes .

1066
01:13:10,800 --> 01:13:14,680
You were tired and disgusted . 11 years !

1067
01:13:15,800 --> 01:13:17,080
You 're human .

1068
01:13:17,640 --> 01:13:20,080
Stop trying to be either a saint or a martyr .

1069
01:13:20,400 --> 01:13:22,880
You probably like thinking it was your fault .

1070
01:13:23,800 --> 01:13:26,240
My sister says I wanted Mother to die .

1071
01:13:27,800 --> 01:13:30,720
I 've wondered ever since if I didn 't wake up in the night ...

1072
01:13:30,760 --> 01:13:34,040
and hear her just go back to sleep .

1073
01:13:35,400 --> 01:13:37,040
It would have been easy .

1074
01:13:37,320 --> 01:13:40,640
- I 've wondered about it . - No , you 're not capable of that .

1075
01:13:41,760 --> 01:13:43,600
You 're a fine person , Eleanor .

1076
01:13:44,160 --> 01:13:46,560
Sensitive and honest and thoroughly good .

1077
01:13:48,680 --> 01:13:51,720
- Do you really think so , John ? - I do indeed .

1078
01:13:55,720 --> 01:13:57,040
Goose bumps .

1079
01:13:58,840 --> 01:14:02,280
There isn 't by any chance a cold spot in this room , too , is there ?

1080
01:14:02,640 --> 01:14:04,280
No , there isn 't .

1081
01:14:20,680 --> 01:14:22,680
" Journeys end in lovers meeting . "

1082
01:14:24,320 --> 01:14:26,360
All I want is to be cherished .

1083
01:14:27,680 --> 01:14:30,400
And here we are listening to that ridiculous harp .

1084
01:14:32,840 --> 01:14:35,640
" Lust . Daughter , preserve thyself .

1085
01:14:37,800 --> 01:14:41,600
" Hold apart from this world , that its lust corrupt thee not .

1086
01:14:41,960 --> 01:14:44,760
" Could you but hear for a moment the agony ...

1087
01:14:45,600 --> 01:14:47,000
" the screaming ... "

1088
01:14:48,000 --> 01:14:49,920
Oh , now , get this , congregation .

1089
01:14:50,280 --> 01:14:52,680
" ... the dreadful crying out of the lustful ...

1090
01:14:52,920 --> 01:14:55,840
" damned for eternity in everlasting flame ! "

1091
01:14:56,720 --> 01:14:59,080
- What have you got there ? - I found it in the library .

1092
01:14:59,160 --> 01:15:00,560
He made it himself .

1093
01:15:00,800 --> 01:15:01,760
Look .

1094
01:15:01,960 --> 01:15:03,720
" Memories for Abigail Lester Crain :

1095
01:15:03,800 --> 01:15:06,000
" A legacy for her education and enlightenment .

1096
01:15:06,080 --> 01:15:08,440
" From her devoted father , Hugh Desmond Lester Crain ...

1097
01:15:08,520 --> 01:15:11,040
" Hill House , October 21 , 1873 . "

1098
01:15:11,760 --> 01:15:15,160
- But that 's today . - Tomorrow and 90 years later .

1099
01:15:15,840 --> 01:15:17,400
Some nursery book , huh ?

1100
01:15:18,240 --> 01:15:21,640
" Honor the authors of thy being , daughter .

1101
01:15:21,880 --> 01:15:24,160
" Thy father and thy mother . "

1102
01:15:25,440 --> 01:15:28,840
Just the thing to give a child at bedtime . No family should be without one .

1103
01:15:28,920 --> 01:15:32,960
I can see him now spitting out the words so they take root in her little mind .

1104
01:15:34,920 --> 01:15:38,080
Hugh Crain , you were a dirty man and you made a dirty house .

1105
01:15:38,240 --> 01:15:40,680
If you can hear me , I 'm telling you to your face ...

1106
01:15:40,760 --> 01:15:43,960
I hope you spend eternity in that foul , rotten book ...

1107
01:15:44,040 --> 01:15:46,120
and never stop burning for a minute .

1108
01:15:50,320 --> 01:15:53,560
- Don 't be a bore , Nell . Sit down and we 'll ... - Leave me alone .

1109
01:15:54,320 --> 01:15:55,840
You are a bore .

1110
01:15:56,520 --> 01:15:58,240
I 've got it . I 'll tear out the pictures ...

1111
01:15:58,320 --> 01:16:01,560
and send them as Christmas cards to my New England relatives .

1112
01:16:01,720 --> 01:16:04,640
I think it 's funny . " Dear Uncle Ned : Merry Christmas , may your soul ... "

1113
01:16:04,720 --> 01:16:06,120
Close that book .

1114
01:16:06,760 --> 01:16:08,520
It 's enough to set anyone 's nerves on edge .

1115
01:16:08,600 --> 01:16:11,280
It 's not the book that 's making our Nell nervous .

1116
01:16:11,400 --> 01:16:13,440
She 's worried about her apartment .

1117
01:16:14,520 --> 01:16:16,840
I didn 't know . Is there anything I can do to help ?

1118
01:16:16,880 --> 01:16:18,560
She thinks she 's being funny .

1119
01:16:18,640 --> 01:16:21,000
Tell me , Dr. Markway , are you fond of stone lions ...

1120
01:16:21,080 --> 01:16:24,000
- the kind you keep on the mantel ? - Shut up , Theo .

1121
01:16:24,080 --> 01:16:26,960
Do you long for a tiny home , something smaller than Hill House ?

1122
01:16:27,040 --> 01:16:28,760
There 's room for two , isn 't there , Nell ?

1123
01:16:28,840 --> 01:16:32,920
You 're a monster , Theo . You 're the monster of Hill House .

1124
01:16:37,440 --> 01:16:39,680
- You 'd better go with her . - Wouldn 't you rather ?

1125
01:16:39,720 --> 01:16:42,960
I said go with her . She shouldn 't be left in that room alone .

1126
01:16:50,040 --> 01:16:51,920
Here you are . Okay , Isolde .

1127
01:16:52,000 --> 01:16:54,080
- Tristan wants you inside . - Leave me alone .

1128
01:16:54,120 --> 01:16:55,840
Stop trying to be the center of attention .

1129
01:16:55,920 --> 01:16:57,960
- Come inside . - You revolt me .

1130
01:16:59,160 --> 01:17:00,960
Can 't you take a joke ?

1131
01:17:01,360 --> 01:17:03,240
I didn 't know you were serious about Markway .

1132
01:17:03,280 --> 01:17:04,880
Of course you did .

1133
01:17:05,480 --> 01:17:07,560
But he shouldn 't be allowed to get away with it .

1134
01:17:07,640 --> 01:17:09,280
Get away with what ?

1135
01:17:09,400 --> 01:17:13,000
- You 're making a fool of yourself over him . - Suppose I 'm not , though .

1136
01:17:13,080 --> 01:17:16,080
You 'd mind terribly if you turned out to be wrong for once .

1137
01:17:16,160 --> 01:17:20,120
- You poor stupid innocent . - I 'd rather be innocent than like you .

1138
01:17:21,160 --> 01:17:22,560
Meaning what ?

1139
01:17:22,720 --> 01:17:24,920
Now who 's being stupid and innocent ?

1140
01:17:25,360 --> 01:17:29,120
- You know perfectly well what I mean . - Is this one of your crazy hallucinations ?

1141
01:17:29,160 --> 01:17:31,240
- I 'm not crazy . - Crazy as a loon .

1142
01:17:31,320 --> 01:17:34,440
You expect me to believe you 're sane and the rest of the world is mad ?

1143
01:17:34,520 --> 01:17:35,920
Why not ?

1144
01:17:36,000 --> 01:17:38,160
The world is full of inconsistencies .

1145
01:17:38,440 --> 01:17:42,600
Unnatural things . " Nature 's mistakes , " they 're called . You , for instance .

1146
01:17:59,080 --> 01:18:01,960
A reporter 's been telephoning all day . He 's on your track .

1147
01:18:02,040 --> 01:18:04,240
- He 's heard about you renting this place . - How ?

1148
01:18:04,320 --> 01:18:06,640
The Dudleys , I bet . They must 've blabbed in town .

1149
01:18:06,720 --> 01:18:08,400
Come back with me now , please .

1150
01:18:08,480 --> 01:18:11,520
If they find out why you 're here , the papers 'll have a field day .

1151
01:18:11,600 --> 01:18:12,960
Who are you ?

1152
01:18:13,320 --> 01:18:14,440
Grace Markway .

1153
01:18:15,840 --> 01:18:17,880
Didn 't John tell you he 's married ?

1154
01:18:18,360 --> 01:18:20,760
- I tried to warn you . - Welcome to our party .

1155
01:18:21,400 --> 01:18:23,000
Who are you ?

1156
01:18:23,200 --> 01:18:25,960
We 're researchers in the field of psychic phenomena .

1157
01:18:26,040 --> 01:18:28,360
Please go . You couldn 't have arrived at a worse time .

1158
01:18:28,440 --> 01:18:30,760
Stop this insanity , John , and come back with me .

1159
01:18:30,840 --> 01:18:31,960
I can 't . Not now .

1160
01:18:32,000 --> 01:18:34,760
I 'm convinced we 're on the verge of a breakthrough .

1161
01:18:35,240 --> 01:18:37,440
Here you are , driver , that 'll be all .

1162
01:18:38,120 --> 01:18:40,400
But I had to come . I had to .

1163
01:18:41,360 --> 01:18:43,240
I 've waited such a long time .

1164
01:18:43,800 --> 01:18:45,640
I 've earned my happiness .

1165
01:18:48,040 --> 01:18:50,400
I was afraid this would be your attitude .

1166
01:18:50,840 --> 01:18:54,200
I 'm not leaving here until you 've got sense enough to leave with me .

1167
01:18:54,280 --> 01:18:56,760
I hope no one minds if I join the ghost hunt .

1168
01:18:57,760 --> 01:19:00,160
All right , I 'll put your things in my room .

1169
01:19:00,840 --> 01:19:03,360
I 'll be very disappointed if I don 't see a ghost .

1170
01:19:03,440 --> 01:19:05,640
Hadn 't you better put me in the ghastly dungeon ...

1171
01:19:05,720 --> 01:19:07,840
or the mysterious secret chamber ?

1172
01:19:07,880 --> 01:19:10,520
There are no dungeons , no secret chambers in Hill House .

1173
01:19:10,560 --> 01:19:12,600
In fact , nothing romantic at all .

1174
01:19:13,080 --> 01:19:15,160
It 's a deadly serious place .

1175
01:19:15,680 --> 01:19:19,080
- Not even a treasure buried in the cellar ? - There 's the nursery .

1176
01:19:20,000 --> 01:19:22,240
Thank you , my dear . The nursery it is .

1177
01:19:32,120 --> 01:19:35,240
You must listen to me . Certain things have happened here .

1178
01:19:35,520 --> 01:19:38,720
You may not believe in the supernatural , but these are physical facts .

1179
01:19:38,760 --> 01:19:41,800
Mrs. Markway , please ...

1180
01:19:42,480 --> 01:19:44,200
Don 't sleep in the nursery .

1181
01:19:44,520 --> 01:19:46,600
I didn 't realize what I was saying .

1182
01:19:47,160 --> 01:19:48,960
You insult my intelligence .

1183
01:19:49,120 --> 01:19:53,200
You don 't think I 'd believe anything you ghost hunters might tell me .

1184
01:19:53,280 --> 01:19:55,640
Even so , you shouldn 't sleep in that room .

1185
01:19:56,160 --> 01:19:58,400
It hasn 't been opened since we 've been here .

1186
01:19:58,480 --> 01:20:02,680
I agree with you about the spook bit , Mrs. M , but it 's true , the air might be bad .

1187
01:20:02,800 --> 01:20:04,160
Oh , poisonous .

1188
01:20:04,360 --> 01:20:07,120
I 've just remembered . No problem .

1189
01:20:07,200 --> 01:20:11,120
I don 't have the key to the nursery , and the Dudleys have gone for the night .

1190
01:20:11,320 --> 01:20:13,600
Incidentally , how 'd you get through the gate ?

1191
01:20:13,680 --> 01:20:16,160
Very supernatural . With a key .

1192
01:20:16,640 --> 01:20:19,040
Your Mrs. Dudley is quite human , I assure you ...

1193
01:20:19,120 --> 01:20:21,240
and not at all averse to a $ 5 bill .

1194
01:20:23,000 --> 01:20:24,280
Hey , look .

1195
01:20:35,360 --> 01:20:38,880
From your expressions , I gather that is the dreaded nursery .

1196
01:20:40,160 --> 01:20:42,720
And as for the bad air , it 's quite the opposite .

1197
01:20:42,800 --> 01:20:44,760
There seems to be a draft .

1198
01:20:45,720 --> 01:20:47,120
Wait a minute , Doc .

1199
01:20:48,760 --> 01:20:51,240
This is ridiculous . Nobody opened these doors .

1200
01:20:51,400 --> 01:20:54,640
That 's right , Luke . You 're beginning to see the light .

1201
01:20:54,760 --> 01:20:56,520
I haven 't seen a damn thing .

1202
01:20:58,560 --> 01:21:00,640
I just don 't like the way it looks .

1203
01:21:02,680 --> 01:21:05,720
Now I know who your fiend of Hill House is .

1204
01:21:05,800 --> 01:21:07,360
The interior decorator .

1205
01:21:07,520 --> 01:21:10,360
Evidently Mrs. Dudley doesn 't get in here very often .

1206
01:21:10,400 --> 01:21:12,800
Looks the same as the rest of the house to me .

1207
01:21:12,840 --> 01:21:15,840
It 's no use , Grace . The air in here is stale .

1208
01:21:16,120 --> 01:21:17,960
I can take care of that .

1209
01:21:18,320 --> 01:21:21,280
Only one way to argue with a woman , Doc . Don 't .

1210
01:21:22,080 --> 01:21:23,640
Good night .

1211
01:21:24,720 --> 01:21:25,880
My mother ...

1212
01:21:31,280 --> 01:21:34,320
This room is the cold , rotten heart of the house .

1213
01:21:34,480 --> 01:21:36,360
Since you 're so foolish , I 'll stay with you .

1214
01:21:36,440 --> 01:21:38,520
But you 're not to be in this room alone tonight .

1215
01:21:38,560 --> 01:21:42,120
I can 't go on watching you waste your life on all this nonsense .

1216
01:21:42,360 --> 01:21:46,240
If there is such a thing as a haunted house , this is my chance to find out .

1217
01:21:46,400 --> 01:21:47,440
All right .

1218
01:21:48,960 --> 01:21:51,480
John , my bag .

1219
01:21:52,400 --> 01:21:54,200
At least leave the door open .

1220
01:21:54,600 --> 01:21:57,560
Don 't worry . I 've brought a special ghost trap with me .

1221
01:22:04,360 --> 01:22:07,760
What if he does have a wife ? I still have a place in this house .

1222
01:22:07,960 --> 01:22:10,920
I belong . I want to stay here .

1223
01:22:11,680 --> 01:22:14,400
It 's the only time anything 's ever happened to me .

1224
01:22:14,880 --> 01:22:18,640
He can 't make me leave , not if Hill House means me to stay .

1225
01:22:19,440 --> 01:22:23,880
Go away , Eleanor , we don 't want you anymore , you can 't stay .

1226
01:22:25,440 --> 01:22:27,320
But I can .

1227
01:22:27,880 --> 01:22:30,080
He doesn 't make the rules around here .

1228
01:22:32,320 --> 01:22:33,720
Nell , I 'm talking to you .

1229
01:22:34,600 --> 01:22:36,000
- I 'm sorry . - What 's the matter ?

1230
01:22:36,040 --> 01:22:37,680
Didn 't you hear Markway ?

1231
01:22:38,440 --> 01:22:39,880
He doesn 't want us to stay here .

1232
01:22:39,960 --> 01:22:42,400
He wants us to spend the night downstairs in the parlor .

1233
01:22:42,480 --> 01:22:45,360
Luke and he will take turns watching on this floor .

1234
01:22:46,360 --> 01:22:48,680
For Pete 's sake , snap out of it .

1235
01:24:23,880 --> 01:24:26,320
- Why aren 't you upstairs ? - I needed a drink .

1236
01:24:50,880 --> 01:24:52,120
- Grace . - Wait a minute .

1237
01:24:58,800 --> 01:25:01,320
It 's nowhere near the nursery , it 's down here .

1238
01:25:12,000 --> 01:25:14,480
It seems to me we 've been on this kick before .

1239
01:25:14,760 --> 01:25:17,320
Next vacation I must really go somewhere else .

1240
01:25:32,720 --> 01:25:35,960
It knows my name . This time it knows my name .

1241
01:25:37,120 --> 01:25:39,040
- I 'll have to go out there . - No !

1242
01:25:40,480 --> 01:25:44,800
- It hasn 't hurt me . Why should it hurt her ? - She might try to do something about it .

1243
01:25:49,000 --> 01:25:50,680
Is it over , Theo ? Is it ?

1244
01:25:51,640 --> 01:25:53,720
No , I 'm so cold .

1245
01:25:54,440 --> 01:25:56,960
It 's going to start everything all over again .

1246
01:26:04,280 --> 01:26:06,840
It can 't get in . Don 't let it get in .

1247
01:26:29,880 --> 01:26:31,640
Oh , God , it knows I 'm here .

1248
01:26:59,160 --> 01:27:01,440
Doc , I 'll let you have the house cheap .

1249
01:27:37,600 --> 01:27:41,160
It will go on and on and come back again until it finds me .

1250
01:27:42,200 --> 01:27:45,520
On and on until it finds me .

1251
01:27:56,480 --> 01:27:57,920
It 's at the nursery .

1252
01:27:58,520 --> 01:28:00,200
- You must be crazy ! - I 'm going out there !

1253
01:28:00,280 --> 01:28:01,800
Not with that thing out there .

1254
01:28:01,880 --> 01:28:04,680
- We have to , Luke . She 's there ! - Don 't be crazy .

1255
01:28:04,760 --> 01:28:06,800
I 've got to find out if Grace is all right .

1256
01:28:06,840 --> 01:28:09,240
I don 't know what it is , but I don 't want to find out ...

1257
01:28:09,280 --> 01:28:12,560
I 've got to get out of here . I 've got to find out if Grace is all right .

1258
01:28:12,600 --> 01:28:14,080
- No , don 't . - Cut it out !

1259
01:28:14,160 --> 01:28:16,400
I 'll come .

1260
01:28:17,720 --> 01:28:19,920
Whatever it wants of me it can have .

1261
01:29:25,040 --> 01:29:27,200
The house is coming down around me .

1262
01:29:27,680 --> 01:29:30,160
The house is destroying itself .

1263
01:29:47,880 --> 01:29:49,280
It 's in the nursery .

1264
01:30:13,560 --> 01:30:14,800
Mrs. Markway ?

1265
01:30:17,400 --> 01:30:18,360
Please .

1266
01:30:23,640 --> 01:30:25,560
Grace , are you ...

1267
01:30:26,640 --> 01:30:27,960
Where is she ?

1268
01:30:29,280 --> 01:30:31,960
- Where is she ? What did you see ? - Nothing .

1269
01:30:33,600 --> 01:30:34,880
She wasn 't here .

1270
01:30:36,080 --> 01:30:37,360
- What happened ? - She 's gone .

1271
01:30:37,440 --> 01:30:38,880
Where ? How ?

1272
01:30:39,040 --> 01:30:40,080
Good God !

1273
01:30:40,160 --> 01:30:42,160
Markway , if this is your idea of a joke ...

1274
01:30:42,240 --> 01:30:44,760
if living in a haunted house has done this to you ...

1275
01:30:44,840 --> 01:30:46,360
We 'll start here , then the whole house .

1276
01:30:46,440 --> 01:30:49,400
- Even if we have to tear the place apart . - You can 't do that .

1277
01:30:49,480 --> 01:30:52,240
If we don 't find her , the police will be around .

1278
01:30:52,320 --> 01:30:55,000
I 'm coming apart , a little at a time .

1279
01:30:59,120 --> 01:31:01,200
Now I know where I 'm going .

1280
01:31:01,680 --> 01:31:05,480
I 'm disappearing inch by inch into this house .

1281
01:31:12,400 --> 01:31:15,720
We killed her . You and I , Hugh Crain .

1282
01:31:49,360 --> 01:31:51,640
She must be around this house somewhere .

1283
01:31:52,640 --> 01:31:54,440
Maybe this whole thing is a bad joke .

1284
01:31:54,480 --> 01:31:57,800
- She isn 't the kind who makes jokes . - You find her , she 's your wife .

1285
01:31:57,840 --> 01:32:00,320
I 'm taking Nell and I 'm clearing out of here .

1286
01:32:00,560 --> 01:32:02,120
Where is Eleanor ?

1287
01:32:15,120 --> 01:32:16,560
I want to stay here .

1288
01:32:17,920 --> 01:32:19,880
I want to stay here always .

1289
01:32:23,440 --> 01:32:25,880
I will not be frightened or alone anymore .

1290
01:32:33,920 --> 01:32:35,760
Has anyone checked outside ?

1291
01:32:37,680 --> 01:32:39,760
Please , Nell , where are you ?

1292
01:32:48,240 --> 01:32:50,960
Here I am , inside .

1293
01:32:51,640 --> 01:32:55,240
It 's not cold at all and the smell is gone .

1294
01:33:23,240 --> 01:33:25,440
I 've broken the spell of Hill House .

1295
01:33:26,320 --> 01:33:27,440
I 'm home .

1296
01:33:33,800 --> 01:33:37,800
No stone lions for me . I am home .

1297
01:35:11,200 --> 01:35:12,320
I will not look back ...

1298
01:35:12,400 --> 01:35:14,960
because then they will know what I am thinking .

1299
01:35:15,280 --> 01:35:17,440
Eleanor , turn around and come down .

1300
01:35:25,160 --> 01:35:26,600
Now , be very , very careful .

1301
01:35:28,920 --> 01:35:30,360
Come down .

1302
01:35:35,880 --> 01:35:38,160
All that is gone and left behind .

1303
01:35:39,400 --> 01:35:41,000
Eleanor , for God 's sake !

1304
01:35:50,160 --> 01:35:54,400
- Wait a minute . This thing will collapse ... - It can 't possibly hold the both of you .

1305
01:36:06,320 --> 01:36:08,000
Just turn around , Eleanor .

1306
01:36:08,600 --> 01:36:11,080
Keep hold of the rail and start down slowly .

1307
01:36:42,120 --> 01:36:43,720
Stand still ! Don 't move !

1308
01:36:46,000 --> 01:36:47,520
Stand perfectly still !

1309
01:36:47,960 --> 01:36:49,920
Nell , do what they say , please !

1310
01:37:26,440 --> 01:37:28,240
I 'm coming on the platform .

1311
01:38:13,240 --> 01:38:14,720
Now come along .

1312
01:38:37,440 --> 01:38:39,240
Are you sure , Eleanor ?

1313
01:38:39,880 --> 01:38:41,400
It was Mrs. Markway .

1314
01:38:42,080 --> 01:38:45,600
Just before I fainted , I looked up , and there she was above the trap door .

1315
01:38:45,640 --> 01:38:47,880
What 's more , she 's still around .

1316
01:38:48,360 --> 01:38:50,920
I don 't know who or what you really saw , Eleanor .

1317
01:38:51,000 --> 01:38:53,600
But whatever it was , we can 't risk letting it happen again .

1318
01:38:53,680 --> 01:38:56,240
- That 's why you 're leaving now . - But I can 't leave now .

1319
01:38:56,320 --> 01:39:00,120
- I brought the car round front . She ready ? - She 's all packed . Take her suitcase .

1320
01:39:00,200 --> 01:39:02,560
No , please , Luke , let me stay .

1321
01:39:02,600 --> 01:39:04,320
I 'll help Mrs. Dudley .

1322
01:39:04,560 --> 01:39:06,720
All it will cost you is just my keep .

1323
01:39:06,920 --> 01:39:09,320
Sorry , honey , but you 're not the type I keep .

1324
01:39:09,400 --> 01:39:12,800
- I can 't leave , I tell you . - I can 't take any more chances .

1325
01:39:13,280 --> 01:39:16,120
I realize now what a terrible thing I was asking of you all .

1326
01:39:16,200 --> 01:39:20,000
You 're leaving as quickly as you can . Then we 'll find Grace or go to the police .

1327
01:39:20,040 --> 01:39:21,280
It isn 't fair .

1328
01:39:21,320 --> 01:39:24,200
I 'm the one who 's supposed to stay here . She 's taken my place .

1329
01:39:24,280 --> 01:39:26,280
Don 't worry . Luke will see you get there safely .

1330
01:39:26,360 --> 01:39:28,960
- Get where ? - Why , home , of course .

1331
01:39:29,040 --> 01:39:32,160
Go back to your own little apartment where all your things are .

1332
01:39:32,240 --> 01:39:33,760
I haven 't any home .

1333
01:39:34,120 --> 01:39:35,320
I made it up .

1334
01:39:36,080 --> 01:39:37,840
No apartment , no things ...

1335
01:39:38,840 --> 01:39:40,880
Everything in all the world that belongs to me ...

1336
01:39:40,960 --> 01:39:43,520
is in that suitcase and a carton in my car .

1337
01:39:44,640 --> 01:39:47,440
So you see , there 's no place you can send me .

1338
01:39:48,000 --> 01:39:49,440
I have to stay here .

1339
01:39:49,600 --> 01:39:51,600
You must have lived somewhere before .

1340
01:39:51,680 --> 01:39:54,440
- You had an address where I wrote you . - My sister 's .

1341
01:39:55,160 --> 01:39:57,440
I sleep on a couch in the living room .

1342
01:39:57,640 --> 01:40:00,520
I 'd be much happier here . I can 't go back to my sister 's .

1343
01:40:00,560 --> 01:40:02,680
Yes , you can , and immediately .

1344
01:40:03,960 --> 01:40:07,440
This is a mistake . Don 't you understand ? The house wants me .

1345
01:40:07,840 --> 01:40:10,200
Mrs. Markway can 't satisfy it . No one else can .

1346
01:40:10,280 --> 01:40:12,000
Forget about this house as soon as you can .

1347
01:40:12,040 --> 01:40:15,680
No , please . I 'm fine now . I 'm not afraid .

1348
01:40:17,360 --> 01:40:18,680
I was happy here .

1349
01:40:19,720 --> 01:40:22,880
- I don 't think Mrs. Markway will be . - Put the bag in the car , Luke .

1350
01:40:22,920 --> 01:40:24,960
Nell is right . Grace is around somewhere .

1351
01:40:25,040 --> 01:40:27,480
- You see ? - Please , there 's no time to waste .

1352
01:40:27,600 --> 01:40:30,960
Please , let me stay . I 'm the only one who can call Mrs. Markway back .

1353
01:40:31,040 --> 01:40:34,080
I was wrong . I should have sent you home the first night .

1354
01:40:37,120 --> 01:40:39,960
This is the only time anything 's ever happened to me .

1355
01:40:45,240 --> 01:40:47,200
I 'm the one it really wants .

1356
01:40:48,920 --> 01:40:52,240
Can 't you feel it ? It 's alive .

1357
01:40:53,440 --> 01:40:54,760
Watching ...

1358
01:40:55,600 --> 01:40:56,920
waiting ...

1359
01:41:00,800 --> 01:41:02,320
Waiting for me .

1360
01:41:07,600 --> 01:41:09,120
I won 't go away .

1361
01:41:09,480 --> 01:41:11,480
You will go away . Right now .

1362
01:41:14,720 --> 01:41:17,080
- No , come on . - I 'll drive . It 's my car .

1363
01:41:18,120 --> 01:41:19,800
At least , half mine .

1364
01:41:20,200 --> 01:41:22,760
All right , let her . I can 't stand here arguing .

1365
01:41:23,200 --> 01:41:25,560
Thank you for rescuing me in the library .

1366
01:41:27,080 --> 01:41:30,320
That was wrong of me , I know , but I 'm all right now , honestly .

1367
01:41:30,400 --> 01:41:33,440
I 'm sorry . I 'm terribly sorry , really .

1368
01:41:37,400 --> 01:41:38,360
Goodbye .

1369
01:41:38,760 --> 01:41:40,320
Let 's get moving .

1370
01:41:47,880 --> 01:41:50,080
I thought you weren 't going to say goodbye .

1371
01:41:50,120 --> 01:41:52,800
Nellie my Nell , be happy , please be happy .

1372
01:41:53,400 --> 01:41:55,200
Everything 's going to be all right .

1373
01:41:55,240 --> 01:41:58,040
I 'm sure Grace is here and we 'll find her . So don 't worry .

1374
01:41:58,120 --> 01:42:00,320
She has my place . It isn 't fair .

1375
01:42:00,760 --> 01:42:02,400
Goodbye , Eleanor .

1376
01:42:06,080 --> 01:42:08,920
I 'll write you . Drive carefully .

1377
01:42:12,400 --> 01:42:13,960
Goodbye .

1378
01:42:17,680 --> 01:42:19,640
Who do I thank for a lovely time ?

1379
01:42:24,040 --> 01:42:25,680
Oh , hold it . Markway !

1380
01:42:29,320 --> 01:42:30,240
The key .

1381
01:42:31,200 --> 01:42:33,760
- To the gate . - Yes , of course .

1382
01:42:34,880 --> 01:42:38,240
What fools they are . The house tricks them so easily .

1383
01:42:38,880 --> 01:42:42,000
Just by telling me to go away , they can 't make me leave .

1384
01:42:42,840 --> 01:42:44,560
They can 't shut me out .

1385
01:42:44,880 --> 01:42:47,120
Not if Hill House means me to stay .

1386
01:42:48,320 --> 01:42:49,920
- Eleanor . - Wait .

1387
01:43:00,680 --> 01:43:02,360
So now I 'm going .

1388
01:43:03,000 --> 01:43:06,360
But I won 't go . Hill House belongs to me .

1389
01:43:09,440 --> 01:43:11,520
I knew it .

1390
01:43:11,960 --> 01:43:13,960
Hill House doesn 't want me to go .

1391
01:43:20,760 --> 01:43:22,960
Stop it . Please . What are you doing ?

1392
01:43:23,480 --> 01:43:24,800
Let go .

1393
01:43:26,600 --> 01:43:28,000
What are you doing ?

1394
01:43:30,040 --> 01:43:33,080
Why don 't they stop me ? Can 't they see what is happening ?

1395
01:43:34,400 --> 01:43:36,680
But it 's happening to you , Eleanor .

1396
01:43:37,280 --> 01:43:40,760
Yes . Something at last is really ...

1397
01:43:43,200 --> 01:43:45,320
really happening to me .

1398
01:44:17,640 --> 01:44:18,960
She 's dead .

1399
01:44:32,200 --> 01:44:35,520
I didn 't want any of this to happen . You must believe me , John .

1400
01:44:36,000 --> 01:44:38,040
What were you doing ? What happened ?

1401
01:44:38,520 --> 01:44:39,960
That terrible house .

1402
01:44:40,560 --> 01:44:44,520
I woke up and I was frightened . So I tried to find your room , but I got lost .

1403
01:44:44,600 --> 01:44:47,360
Almost as though the house were doing it on purpose .

1404
01:44:47,400 --> 01:44:49,120
And I ended up in the attic .

1405
01:44:49,160 --> 01:44:52,120
I was only trying to find a way out when I opened the trap door .

1406
01:44:52,200 --> 01:44:54,200
I wasn 't trying to frighten her .

1407
01:44:54,280 --> 01:44:57,600
- Didn 't you see me ? - No , but Eleanor did .

1408
01:44:58,160 --> 01:45:00,200
The shock of seeing you almost killed her .

1409
01:45:00,280 --> 01:45:01,360
She did kill her .

1410
01:45:02,480 --> 01:45:05,080
Seeing her is what made Eleanor lose control of the car .

1411
01:45:05,160 --> 01:45:08,640
No . She only saw me the very last instant .

1412
01:45:08,720 --> 01:45:10,840
The same time I saw her .

1413
01:45:11,480 --> 01:45:13,640
I don 't even know how I got out here .

1414
01:45:14,120 --> 01:45:15,600
It wasn 't your fault .

1415
01:45:16,680 --> 01:45:18,360
Eleanor did it to herself .

1416
01:45:19,080 --> 01:45:21,040
It looked to me , anyway , like she ...

1417
01:45:21,120 --> 01:45:23,480
deliberately aimed the car at this tree .

1418
01:45:24,640 --> 01:45:28,240
Where the first Mrs. Crain was also killed in an " accident . "

1419
01:45:30,040 --> 01:45:31,360
Here 's the mark .

1420
01:45:34,040 --> 01:45:36,800
There was something in the car with her , I 'm sure of it .

1421
01:45:36,840 --> 01:45:39,640
Call it what you like , but Hill House is haunted .

1422
01:45:40,640 --> 01:45:43,520
It didn 't want her to leave , and her poor bedeviled mind ...

1423
01:45:43,560 --> 01:45:45,560
wasn 't strong enough to fight it .

1424
01:45:47,080 --> 01:45:49,640
- Poor Eleanor . - Maybe not " poor " Eleanor .

1425
01:45:51,200 --> 01:45:53,760
It was what she wanted , to stay here .

1426
01:45:55,120 --> 01:45:56,920
She had no place else to go .

1427
01:45:58,600 --> 01:46:01,040
The house belongs to her now , too .

1428
01:46:01,600 --> 01:46:03,000
Maybe she 's happier .

1429
01:46:03,680 --> 01:46:05,240
You wait here , Grace .

1430
01:46:05,320 --> 01:46:07,800
I 'll go and get your things and call the police .

1431
01:46:07,840 --> 01:46:10,720
No one must go in that house again . Whatever is there might ...

1432
01:46:10,760 --> 01:46:12,160
I 'll be all right .

1433
01:46:12,880 --> 01:46:16,680
The house has what it wants ... for a while .

1434
01:46:24,520 --> 01:46:28,360
It ought to be burned down and the ground sowed with salt .

1435
01:46:33,880 --> 01:46:38,200
Hill House has stood for 90 years and might stand for 90 more .

1436
01:46:39,120 --> 01:46:43,200
Within , walls continue upright , bricks meet ...

1437
01:46:43,800 --> 01:46:47,600
floors are firm , and doors are sensibly shut .

1438
01:46:48,600 --> 01:46:52,280
Silence lies steadily against the wood and stone of Hill House .

1439
01:46:52,640 --> 01:46:56,440
And we who walk here walk alone .

